WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.740 --> 00:02:09.000
[Music]

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:19.620
[Car pulls up to house.]

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:30.900
[People laughing and chatting.]

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.566
[Ellen:] I guess we beat the Goodbodys here.

00:02:32.566 --> 00:02:33.966
[Leona:] Who?

00:02:33.966 --> 00:02:35.266
[Charlie:] The Goodbodys, the chaperones.

00:02:35.266 --> 00:02:38.360
[Leona:] Oh yes, the Goodbodys, don't worry, 
they'll be along.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:43.360
[Charlie:] There. Here we are, the Mitchell ski 
lodge, everybody welcome.

00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:45.066
[Leona:] Ooooh, let's get the fire going.

00:02:45.066 --> 00:02:49.599
[Charlie:] Right. The fireplace is laid, Ben, you light 
it, will ya, I'll see to the kitchen stove.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.600
[Dr. Ben:] Okay.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.633
[Ladies glance at the two doors that read Guys, 
Gals.]

00:03:00.633 --> 00:03:04.766
[Leona:] Oh, those are the bunk rooms.
One lot for the gals and one lot for the guys.

00:03:04.766 --> 00:03:08.966
All quite respectable. 
Oh, match, doctor?

00:03:08.966 --> 00:03:10.299
[Dr. Ben:] Oh thanks, Miss Ware.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.533
[Leona:] Not at all, Dr. Edwards.

00:03:12.533 --> 00:03:14.599
[Charlie:] Leona, come give me a hand, will you?

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:20.200
[Leona:] Okay. Miss Carver, will you kindly help Dr. 
Edwards while I go and assist Mr. Mitchell?

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.666
[Chuckles]

00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:26.132
[Dr. Ben:] Well, I guess it had better be Ellen and 
Ben.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:31.533
[Ellen:] I guess so. Like skiing, doctor? Ben. 
Hahaha.

00:03:31.533 --> 00:03:34.766
[Dr. Ben:] Yes, very much, but I don't get much of 
an opportunity.

00:03:34.766 --> 00:03:38.820
[Ellen:] We're not healthy enough in Melton? Is our 
new health officer overworked?

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:43.433
[Dr. Ben:] Yes, to the first question.

00:03:43.433 --> 00:03:59.866
[Music]

00:03:59.866 --> 00:04:01.266
[Dr. Ben:] Beautiful night.

00:04:01.266 --> 00:04:04.466
[Charlie:] Beautiful whiskey here. Why don't you 
two have some?

00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:05.840
[Dr. Ben:] No thanks, not just now.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.160
[Ellen:] I'm happy with the coffee.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.560
[Charlie:] Mustn't carry this health business too far, doctor.

00:04:11.566 --> 00:04:15.166
[Leona:] If he doesn't want to drink, he doesn't. 
Ellen never drinks anyway.

00:04:15.166 --> 00:04:19.732
[Charlie:] Good for Ben to loosen up a little. Takes 
life too seriously.  People resent that, you know.

00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:21.066
[Dr. Ben:] Do they?

00:04:21.066 --> 00:04:23.599
[Charlie:] Some people. Like Jeff Curran, for 
instance.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.266
[Dr. Ben:] What about Curran?

00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:27.266
[Leona:] The alderman?

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:30.432
[Charlie:] The same. You've been on the job for 
two months now Ben,

00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:32.499
and you've got Curran down on you.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.200
He's out to get you. So the grapevine tells me.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.566
[Ellen:] What is all this Charlie?

00:04:37.566 --> 00:04:41.799
[Charlie:] Well, Ben closed up a ratty little 
restaurant in the south end, unsanitary.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.866
Curran owns it.

00:04:43.866 --> 00:04:48.932
So when Ben proposes that all civic employees 
should be given blood tests,

00:04:48.933 --> 00:04:54.233
Curran persuades the mayor, my esteemed father, 
that this is an insulting slander

00:04:54.233 --> 00:05:01.333
against old and honored citizens of the community. 
The mayor listens. He always listens to Curran.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.933
[Leona:] Blood tests?

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:06.520
[Charlie:] To discover what we delicately refer to as 
the social diseases, my dear.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.833
[Leona:] Ooooh.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.400
[Dr. Ben:] Let's drop the subject, Charlie.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.160
[Charlie:] Okay, but take my tip and go easy, my 
friend.

00:05:12.166 --> 00:05:14.699
Politicians don't like crusaders.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.800
[Ellen:] Some politicians are crusaders.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.866
[Charlie:] Whoops, I guess I put my foot in it.

00:05:18.866 --> 00:05:20.999
[Leona:] What about some skiing?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.466
[Ellen:] It's late.

00:05:22.466 --> 00:05:27.532
[Dr. Ben:] Oh, it's only, uh...
Say, what happened to the Goodbodys?

00:05:27.533 --> 00:05:29.899
[Charlie and Leona laugh.]

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.400
[Charlie:] They arrived hours ago. They're here.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.766
[Ellen:] Here.

00:05:32.766 --> 00:05:34.066
[Dr. Ben:] Where?

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:36.200
[Leona:] Us. We're the good bodies, all four of us.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.800
[Charlie:] Get it? Good bodies.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.300
We're going to be good boys and girls, so we don't need a chaperone.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.700
Now don't tell me you had any other intentions. Naughty, naughty.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.433
[Dr. Ben:] Your jokes aren't very funny, Charlie.

00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:51.699
[Leona:] Aww, now Ellen, don't be mad.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.700
We didn't want any of those killjoys around,
and we knew

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.966
you wouldn't come unless there were chaperones.

00:05:55.966 --> 00:06:01.966
[Charlie:] Gee whiz, why does everybody have to 
be so stuffy?

00:06:01.966 --> 00:06:27.800
[Music as Dr. Ben walks out to the porch.]

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.260
[Ellen:] The pale, cold beauty of winter's mantle.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.633
[Dr. Ben:] What's that from?

00:06:43.633 --> 00:06:45.466
[Ellen:] From a book of poems I have.

00:06:45.466 --> 00:06:46.799
[Dr. Ben:] I'd like to read them sometime.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.860
[Ellen:] I'll lend it to you. 
It's so fresh and clean out here.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.900
[Dr. Ben:] Yes, Charlie's sense of humor is .....well.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.666
[Ellen:] Maybe I am a little stuffy.

00:06:57.666 --> 00:07:00.332
[Dr. Ben:] The chaperone business bother you?

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:03.500
[Ellen:] Not really.  
It's just Charlie's attitude, and Leona's.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.933
Think I'm being a Victorian?

00:07:05.933 --> 00:07:09.966
[Dr. Ben:] If you are, that makes two of us. 
Like to go skiing?

00:07:09.966 --> 00:07:11.999
[Ellen:] Getting pretty late, isn't it?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.566
[Dr. Ben:] I guess it is.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:16.199
[Ellen:] Wasted trip, no skiing.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.466
[Dr. Ben:] I didn't say it was wasted.

00:07:18.466 --> 00:07:20.366
[Ellen:] Should we go in?
[Dr. Ben:] Cold?

00:07:20.366 --> 00:07:25.500
[Ellen:] No.
[Dr. Ben:] Let's go for a walk down the road.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:44.980
[Music swells as Charlie and Leona kiss on the couch.]

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.120
[Charlie:] Leona.
[Leona:] Don't.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.700
[Charlie:] What's the matter with you?
[Leona:] You're so rough.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.933
Why can't you kiss me nicely!

00:07:54.933 --> 00:07:56.866
[Charlie:] Nicely!

00:07:56.866 --> 00:08:02.866
[Leona runs off to the bedroom crying.]

00:08:02.866 --> 00:08:09.932
[Dr. Ben and Ellen return from walk.]

00:08:09.933 --> 00:08:13.066
[Charlie:] Been skiing?
[Ellen:] No, walking.

00:08:13.066 --> 00:08:15.232
[Dr. Ben:] You should have come along with us, 
Charlie.

00:08:15.233 --> 00:08:19.833
[Charlie:] I'll say I should have.

00:08:19.833 --> 00:08:22.666
[Dr. Ben:] Ellen and I feel we should go back to 
town, Charlie.

00:08:22.666 --> 00:08:25.199
[Charlie:] Okay, let's be proper by all means.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.940
[Ellen:] I'll tell Leona.

00:08:31.166 --> 00:08:34.200
[Sounds of car engine, straining to start]

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.866
[Leona:] That battery sounds awfully weak.

00:08:35.866 --> 00:08:37.599
[Ellen:] This would happen.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.120
[Leona:] Oh really Ellen, all this fuss.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.040
[Dr. Ben:] All right Charlie, try it once more.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:48.580
[Engine sounds]

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:59.300
[Charlie:] Look, Ben, you fix this blasted thing.  
I'm staying, I'll get a bus down tomorrow.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.260
And Leona can do what she likes.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:19.320
[Dr. Ben:] That battery is completely shot now.

00:09:19.333 --> 00:09:22.333
[Charlie:] Well, you three can walk 50 miles to Melton, I'm going to bed.

00:09:22.333 --> 00:09:26.399
Good night.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.933
[Leona:] I'm not walking anywhere. 
Charlie's right.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:31.980
All this silly nonsense.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.460
[Ellen:] What are we going to do?

00:09:34.466 --> 00:09:38.299
[Dr. Ben:] Well, it's quite a hike to Melton, even for 
a couple of starchy Victorians.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.900
[Ellen:] Well, good night.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.480
[Dr. Ben:] Good night.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:11.500
[Music]

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.440
[Dr. Ben:] Mr. Williams

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.433
[Mr. Williams:] How do you do, Dr. Edwards?

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:17.080
[Dr. Ben:] Won't you sit down?  
[Mr. Williams:] Thanks.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:21.680
[Dr. Ben:] What can I do for you?
[Mr. Williams:] No, what can I do for you?

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.733
[Dr. Ben:] I don't know what you mean.

00:10:23.733 --> 00:10:25.166
[Mr. Williams:] Well, I want to cooperate.

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.266
I just heard about how you closed up that 
place of Curran's.

00:10:28.266 --> 00:10:32.632
That was a good move. 
Anything that improves this town is okay by me.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:38.600
I'm way ahead of most places in Melton. 
You know my club, clean in every respect.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:43.620
Now why can't all public places be like that?
No reason at all.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.033
[Dr. Ben:] Agreed. So?
[Mr. Williams:] I'd like to cooperate.

00:10:47.033 --> 00:10:49.933
[Dr. Ben:] That's very public-spirited of you.

00:10:49.933 --> 00:10:54.666
[Mr. Williams:] Now don't think that I can't help. 
I meet people see, in the club, outside.

00:10:54.666 --> 00:10:58.166
I know everybody in Melton, and I've got plenty of 
influence.

00:10:58.166 --> 00:10:59.766
[Dr. Ben:] Probably you have, Mr. Williams,

00:10:59.766 --> 00:11:04.166
but just what do you think you can do for this 
department?

00:11:04.166 --> 00:11:06.632
[Mr. Williams:] Well, I thought maybe you were 
planning on some sort of

00:11:06.633 --> 00:11:08.233
"Clean Up Melton" campaign.

00:11:08.233 --> 00:11:11.999
If you are figuring on such a campaign, maybe I 
can get behind you.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.366
[Dr. Ben:] Possibly. I appreciate your interest, and 
perhaps there is a way than you can help.

00:11:17.366 --> 00:11:19.932
[Mr. Williams:] You name it, doc, and it's done.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.360
[Dr. Ben:] Come here.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.760
[They walk over to a map.]

00:11:25.766 --> 00:11:30.766
[Dr. Ben:] This shaded area on the map represents 
one of the worst slums in Melton.

00:11:30.766 --> 00:11:36.166
If you can use your influence to help clear up 
those slums, it would be a great service.

00:11:36.166 --> 00:11:39.532
Should be easy for you since you own most of 
those buildings.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.780
[Mr. Williams:] Really, doctor, you seem to know a 
great deal about my affairs.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:49.360
[Dr. Ben:] That's my job, and I'm telling you, Mr. 
Williams, if you don't clean up those slums, I will.

00:11:54.740 --> 00:12:03.160
[Lively music]

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.960
[Patsy:] Marty?

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:10.833
[Mr. Williams:] I'm thinking.
[Patsy:] Oh, I'm going home.

00:12:10.833 --> 00:12:12.799
Oh, Marty what's come over you?

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:16.566
If you're tired of me, just tell me, but don't freeze up on 
me like this.

00:12:16.566 --> 00:12:18.780
[Mr. Williams] Oh, lay off will ya?

00:12:20.766 --> 00:12:24.160
[Patsy:] You want me to come up to your place 
tonight?

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.920
No, I suppose not.

00:12:27.933 --> 00:12:30.999
[Mr. Williams:] Now what are you worrying about,
I'm just as nuts about you as ever.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.040
I'm busy, that's all.
I got things on my mind.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.220
Your old man, beat it.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:47.520
[Mr. Curran:] Was that Patsy?
[Mr. Williams:] Patsy?

00:12:48.084 --> 00:12:50.404
No, maybe you saw Maura, the hat-check girl.

00:12:54.888 --> 00:12:56.348
[Mr. Curran:] Are you seeing that Edwards guy 
today?

00:12:56.348 --> 00:12:57.808
[Mr. Williams:] This afternoon.
[Mr. Curran:] Well.

00:12:58.368 --> 00:13:00.868
[Mr. Williams:] Hope to make trouble, I figure.
[Mr. Curran:] What'd he say?

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:04.166
[Mr. Williams:] Not much except to suggest I clean 
up the slums I own on the south side.

00:13:04.166 --> 00:13:05.899
If I don't, he will.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:09.033
[Mr. Curran:] That all?
[Mr. Williams:] That's all he said.

00:13:09.033 --> 00:13:11.666
[Mr. Curran:] If he gets too busy we'll take care of 
him.

00:13:11.666 --> 00:13:18.866
I have Shorty here keeping tabs on him. 
Look Marty, you leave Patsy alone.

00:13:18.866 --> 00:13:22.166
I know you're playing around with her; leave her 
alone!

00:13:22.166 --> 00:13:24.566
[Mr. Williams:] She drops in, no harm in that.

00:13:24.566 --> 00:13:27.788
[Mr. Curran:] I don't want her having anything to do 
with you.

00:13:29.366 --> 00:13:31.308
[Shorty:] Marty?
[Mr. Williams:] What do you want?

00:13:31.333 --> 00:13:34.299
[Shorty:] The boss got me watching Patsy, too.
[Mr. Williams:] What?

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.966
[Shorty:] Don't get sore Marty, don't get sore. 
I'm only doing my duty, see.

00:13:37.966 --> 00:13:44.032
Now suppose you slip me a fiver every now and 
then, I don't even see Patsy at all here.

00:13:44.033 --> 00:13:47.299
[Mr. Williams:] Okay, make it five a week.
[Shorty:] That's swell.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.566
[Mr. Williams:] Just deduct it from the $200 you owe 
me.

00:13:49.566 --> 00:13:53.199
[Shorty:] Well, what do you know? I double-crossed 
myself.

00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:56.148
[Mr. Curran:] Shorty!
[Shorty:] Coming, boss.

00:13:59.466 --> 00:14:00.808
[Patsy slides back into booth]

00:14:00.833 --> 00:14:02.099
[Patsy:] Well, how do you like that?

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:05.666
Who does he think he is pulling his heavy father 
act on me?

00:14:05.666 --> 00:14:08.408
He's done nothing but snarl at me all my life.

00:14:12.632 --> 00:14:17.766
[Mayor:] Naturally, you'll find your blemish in any 
community, but, on the whole, I'd say that Melton

00:14:17.766 --> 00:14:22.332
was one of the healthiest, most up-to-date little 
towns anywhere on this continent.

00:14:22.333 --> 00:14:25.133
Certainly one of the most go-ahead, 
I know that for certain.

00:14:25.133 --> 00:14:29.699
Of course, I haven't worked alone. 
We're a team here in Melton.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.533
And you know the secret of our success, Dr. 
Edwards?

00:14:32.533 --> 00:14:38.033
Patience and caution. 
Go slowly and go solidly.

00:14:38.033 --> 00:14:40.133
That is our motto.

00:14:40.133 --> 00:14:43.833
[Charlie:] End of lecture, father?
[Mayor:] Don't be impertinent, Charles.

00:14:43.833 --> 00:14:47.933
Oh by George, I must be getting along. 
It's nearly 9 o'clock, got a committee meeting.

00:14:47.933 --> 00:14:50.666
Well, it was nice to have seen you, doctor.

00:14:50.666 --> 00:14:55.966
We must get together more often...keep each 
other informed.

00:14:55.966 --> 00:14:57.966
I shall be late, my dear.

00:14:57.966 --> 00:15:03.332
Good night to you all, and the most stimulating 
conversation, doctor.

00:15:03.332 --> 00:15:06.588
[Charlie:] Father just loves stimulating 
conversation, Ben.

00:15:09.099 --> 00:15:12.888
I'll say this though, he's smooth.  
That was a sugar-coated lecture, Ben.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:14.766
[Mrs. Mayor:] What are you talking about?

00:15:14.766 --> 00:15:18.299
[Charlie:] Ben was just warned to be a good boy or 
he'd be dropped from the team.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:22.066
It's as simple as that. 
Curran has been needling his honor, I'll say.

00:15:22.066 --> 00:15:25.766
[Mrs. Mayor:] Charlie, you talk in riddles.
[Dr. Ben:] He probably means very well.

00:15:25.766 --> 00:15:30.466
[Charlie:] Always think the best, eh?  
Good ole Mr. Goodbody.

00:15:30.466 --> 00:15:31.866
Still touchy about that?

00:15:31.866 --> 00:15:34.332
Ben and Ellen thought it was dreadfully immoral

00:15:34.333 --> 00:15:37.133
not to have a chaperone at the lodge last 
weekend.

00:15:37.133 --> 00:15:40.833
[Mrs. Mayor:] Really?
[Dr. Ben:] Charlie exaggerates.

00:15:40.833 --> 00:15:44.466
[Mrs. Mayor:] Chaperones are so outdated.
[Dr. Ben:] Are they?

00:15:44.466 --> 00:15:48.299
[Mrs. Mayor:] Well now, don't tell me you're as old-
fashioned as that, Dr. Edwards.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:52.933
Why, when I think of the harm done by chaperones 
and stern parents...

00:15:52.933 --> 00:15:54.666
[Dr. Ben:] Harm?

00:15:54.668 --> 00:15:58.766
[Mrs. Mayor:] Yes harm. Policing people is useless, 
doesn't do any good.

00:15:58.766 --> 00:16:01.608
[Dr. Ben:] Sometimes they need guidance.

00:16:03.548 --> 00:16:06.468
[Dr. Ben knocks on the door.]

00:16:14.388 --> 00:16:17.848
[Daphne:] Having fun?
[Dr. Ben:] Good evening. I wonder if you could ...

00:16:17.866 --> 00:16:25.799
[Daphne:] Come in, it's cold out there.
[Dr. Ben:] Is Miss Carver at home?

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.933
[Daphne:] Nope, the concert. Who are you?
[Dr. Ben:] Dr. Edwards. I just came to return ...

00:16:28.933 --> 00:16:32.166
[Daphne:] That Edwards?
Let me have your coat.

00:16:32.166 --> 00:16:35.032
[Dr. Ben:] Ben Edwards. I don't think I'll really stay.

00:16:35.033 --> 00:16:37.466
[Daphne:] Why won't you stay? You came calling, 
didn't you?

00:16:37.466 --> 00:16:39.166
[Dr. Ben:] Well, not really.

00:16:39.166 --> 00:16:43.299
[Dorothy:] Men always think they have to have 
some excuse, Ellen ain't in...

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:46.000
[Dr. Ben:] Yes...
Howard and Marian are in though,

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.200
and they'll be glad to see you. 
Nice folks.

00:16:48.208 --> 00:17:02.628
Go and sit Ben. Marian! Howard!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.720
Be here in a second.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.760
[Howard Carter:] Hello there!

00:17:19.766 --> 00:17:23.199
I've been fixing laundry tubs for Daphne.
Glad to see you.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.000
[Dr. Ben:] Good evening.
[Marian:] Well, how nice!

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.866
[Dr. Ben:] Good evening. You're ahh...

00:17:27.866 --> 00:17:30.866
[Daphne:] Howard and Marian Carter, Ellen's 
parents.

00:17:30.866 --> 00:17:33.580
Ben Edwards, doctor.

00:17:33.766 --> 00:17:36.920
[Howard:] We're a bit informal around here,  
Daphne's influence.

00:17:36.933 --> 00:17:42.366
I hired her ages ago as my housekeeper,
and she's been running our lives ever since.

00:17:42.366 --> 00:17:45.299
[Marian:] That was Daphne by the way. 
Please sit down, Dr. Edwards.

00:17:45.299 --> 00:17:47.728
[Dr. Ben:] Thank you.

00:17:52.266 --> 00:17:54.248
[Howard:] I knew you the minute you turned 
around,

00:17:54.266 --> 00:17:57.599
saw your picture in the paper when you came to 
town.

00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:01.100
[Marian:] And Ellen has told us about you.
[Dr. Ben:] Oh yes, that weekend.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.960
[Marian:] Oh, I didn't mean that. 
Although it was so foolish of Charlie and Leona.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:10.760
[Howards:] Not the fault of you and Ellen at all. 
So you tackled Jeff Curran, eh?

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:17.980
Let me shake your hand again, Dr. Edwards. 
Let's get acquainted.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.966
Tell me all about this Curran affair.

00:18:19.966 --> 00:18:26.020
[Dr. Ben:] So you see it's like trying to kill a weed 
by mowing it down:

00:18:26.566 --> 00:18:30.200
You destroy it here, and it grows up again 
someplace else.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:33.800
That's all we doctors and hospitals and social 
workers can do.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:39.560
Mow down the single manifestations of disease 
and delinquency, but it takes group action,

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:44.020
community action, to uproot these weeds and 
completely destroy them.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:49.200
Oh gosh, I appear to have been babbling for 
hours.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:53.000
[Marian:] You haven't been babbling, Ben. 
You've been talking sense.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.200
[Howard:] I see what you mean, Ben.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.100
As principal of the high school and a member of 
the city council,

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:02.066
perhaps I'm a mower, too, instead of an uprooter. 
[Dr. Ben:] I didn't mean ...

00:19:02.066 --> 00:19:05.499
[Howard:] No, it could be true though. You've 
missed something, Ellen.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:08.700
[Dr. Ben:] Hello, how long have you been here?
[Ellen:] Oh, not long.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:11.866
I'm sorry I'm so late.  
Went down to the station to see Leona off.

00:19:11.866 --> 00:19:14.966
[Marian:] Is she going away?
[Ellen:] Just to the city for a few days, that's all.

00:19:14.966 --> 00:19:17.299
Charlie drove me home. He wouldn't come in 
though.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:20.366
Rushed off somewhere. Please sit down, Ben.

00:19:20.366 --> 00:19:23.466
[Dr. Ben:] Oh, it must be getting very late.
[Marian:] Not too late for a cup of tea.

00:19:23.466 --> 00:19:26.866
[Howard:] Yeah, let's have a cup of tea.
[Marian:] I'll go put the kettle on.

00:19:26.866 --> 00:19:33.732
[Daphne:] It'll be ready in a few shakes.  
My, this fellow Ben sure does talk, don't he.

00:19:33.732 --> 00:19:38.328
[Marian:] Daphne, you are a wonderful woman.

00:19:38.328 --> 00:20:25.248
[Couples dance as music plays.]

00:20:25.266 --> 00:20:30.032
[Patsy:] Mind if I sit down here?
[Charlie:] Gee no, I mean please do. Have a drink.

00:20:30.033 --> 00:20:31.633
[Patsy:] Nope.

00:20:31.633 --> 00:20:33.799
[Charlie:] What's the matter, mad about 
something?

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:38.166
[Patsy:] No. Where's your little girlfriend tonight?
[Charlie:] Gone to the city.

00:20:38.166 --> 00:20:40.966
[Patsy:] So the mouse is playing, eh?
[Charlie:] Could be.

00:20:40.966 --> 00:20:43.166
[Patsy:] Mmmhmm.

00:20:43.166 --> 00:20:53.766
[Charlie:] Gee, that's quite a bracelet you've got.  
Let me see.

00:21:01.966 --> 00:21:04.566
[Patsy:] You know, if you take me somewhere else, 
I'd love to have a drink.

00:21:04.566 --> 00:21:06.099
I'm sick to death of this place.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.266
[Charlie:] Okay fine, I know where we can go.
[Patsy:] Where?

00:21:08.266 --> 00:21:11.699
[Charlie:] Some place nice and quiet. My ski lodge.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:15.533
[Patsy:] Oh no, that's miles away and, besides...

00:21:15.533 --> 00:21:16.833
I want a drink.

00:21:16.833 --> 00:21:18.999
[Charlie:] Okay, we'll take a drink with us.  
Where's Marty?

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:25.966
Marty, come here. 
How about a bottle to go, Marty?

00:21:25.966 --> 00:21:27.532
Can you get one from Joe?

00:21:27.533 --> 00:21:32.666
[Marty:] Sure, why not?
[Patsy:] Sure, why not?

00:21:32.666 --> 00:21:34.120
[Charlie:] Atta girl.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:48.860
[Shorty:] Marty.
[Marty:] I thought you quit hanging around here.

00:21:48.866 --> 00:21:51.932
[Shorty:] I gotta look as though I'm on the job. 
Hey Marty, whatta I do now.

00:21:51.933 --> 00:21:55.766
The boss said about you and Patsy, 
not Patsy and anybody else.

00:21:55.766 --> 00:21:58.532
[Mr. Williams:] Skip it.
[Shorty:] Okay, okay.

00:21:58.533 --> 00:22:02.399
I got something for you on that doctor guy.
[Mr. Williams:] Yeah, what?

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:05.866
[Shorty:] Our boy Benny is a man about town,
a fast guy with the chicks, see.

00:22:05.866 --> 00:22:08.899
He spent last weekend with Ellen Carter up in the Mitchell ski lodge.

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:14.766
Course this doll Leona Webb and young Charlie 
is there too, but nobody else....

00:22:14.766 --> 00:22:18.166
[Mr. Williams:] You sure of this?
[Shorty:] Am I sure? Am I sure?

00:22:18.166 --> 00:22:21.699
Didn't I get it from my brother-in-law,
who's married to my third sister,

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:23.400
the one with the wart?

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.733
He runs the garage up in the mountains, see.

00:22:25.733 --> 00:22:29.133
Last Sunday, he's called out
to the Mitchell ski lodge to start a car.

00:22:29.133 --> 00:22:32.266
He figures out the whole deal, and he gives me a call.

00:22:32.266 --> 00:22:34.066
We got an arrangement, see.

00:22:34.066 --> 00:22:36.999
Lots of monkey business going on 
in those ski lodges.

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:39.766
Da louse, he wants a cut. 
And everything he makes her do...

00:22:39.766 --> 00:22:43.866
Well, can you use it?

00:22:43.866 --> 00:22:46.600
[Mr. Williams:] I can use it.

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:56.833
[Charlie and Patsy up at the ski lodge]

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:58.100
[Patsy:] Whew.

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:00.860
[Charlie:] Hang on a second. 
I'll light the lantern and start a fire.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:34.080
[Patsy:] Ahhhh, I think I've got a cold.

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:40.220
[Charlie:] I'll keep you warm.

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:51.080
You don't mind being kissed roughly, do you?

00:23:57.740 --> 00:24:01.533
[Dr. Ben:] Good morning, gentlemen.
[Howard:] Good morning, Ben.

00:24:01.533 --> 00:24:03.166
You know Tom McAllister?

00:24:03.166 --> 00:24:04.532
[Tom McAllister:] Yes, we've met.

00:24:04.533 --> 00:24:05.833
[Dr. Ben:] Is this an official visit?

00:24:05.833 --> 00:24:09.033
You fellows look very businesslike this morning.
Anything wrong?

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:12.660
[Howard:] Plenty. Read this.

00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:16.140
The marked item near the bottom.

00:24:26.933 --> 00:24:28.799
[Dr. Ben:] The filthy rotten....

00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:32.900
Operator, operator, get me the office of The Magpie.

00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:34.333
[Tom McAllister:] What are you going to do?

00:24:34.333 --> 00:24:36.299
[Dr. Ben:] I'm going to tell this editor 
that he has a libel suit on his hands.

00:24:36.300 --> 00:24:38.900
[Howard:] Don't be a fool.  
What good would that do?

00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:41.366
[Dr. Ben:] You can't knuckle under to stuff like this.

00:24:41.366 --> 00:24:42.899
[Howard:] For heaven's sake,
think of Ellen, will you?

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:44.233
[Dr. Ben:] That's who I'm thinking of!

00:24:44.233 --> 00:24:45.966
[Tom McAllister:] No one is asking 
you to knuckle under.

00:24:45.966 --> 00:24:47.740
We want you to fight.

00:24:51.766 --> 00:24:53.960
[Dr. Ben:] What are we going to do?

00:24:53.966 --> 00:24:57.100
[Howard:] About that, ignore it.

00:24:58.380 --> 00:25:02.200
Can you see yourself and Ellen 
being cross-examined by their lawyers?

00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:03.833
[Dr. Ben:] Oh, look here Carter, it 
will never come to that ....

00:25:03.833 --> 00:25:09.066
[Howard:] My dear young chap, I know my 
daughter, and I've come to know you and like you.

00:25:09.066 --> 00:25:13.240
All I mean is you can't walk in mud
without being smeared.

00:25:14.166 --> 00:25:16.860
It's not worth it for the sake of exposing a cheap 
lie.

00:25:18.600 --> 00:25:20.600
[Dr. Ben:] Well...

00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:25.833
[Howard:] I got mad too when I read that thing.
Then I talked to Mac.

00:25:25.833 --> 00:25:28.566
He opened my eyes.

00:25:28.566 --> 00:25:30.399
[Tom McAllister:] This is more than a scandal, Ben.

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:34.166
Nasty little items like that are sold at a fat profit to the people concerned.

00:25:34.166 --> 00:25:35.832
No one approached you?

00:25:35.833 --> 00:25:39.433
[Dr. Ben:] No.
[Tom McAllister:] Nor Howard.

00:25:39.433 --> 00:25:40.733
Why not?

00:25:40.733 --> 00:25:43.833
Someone wanted that printed to discredit you, I'd 
say.

00:25:43.833 --> 00:25:44.300
[Dr. Ben:] But why?

00:25:44.300 --> 00:25:48.500
[Tom McAllister:] Well, you've made enemies.  
Made people uncomfortable. May do it again.

00:25:48.500 --> 00:25:52.833
[Dr. Ben:] Curran? Williams?
[Tom McAllister:] Likely. It doesn't matter who, really.

00:25:52.833 --> 00:25:59.133
[Howard:] Don't you see, this is more than a slur.
It's a challenge from the racketeer element.

00:25:59.133 --> 00:26:01.933
[Dr. Ben:] Well, that's a little farfetched.
[Tom McAllister:] I don't think so.

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:04.340
Someone is out to get you.

00:26:05.140 --> 00:26:08.300
[Dr. Ben:] What are we going to do about it?
[Tom McAllister:] We fight back.

00:26:08.300 --> 00:26:11.300
After all, it's time we drove the racketeers out of this town.

00:26:11.300 --> 00:26:14.133
[Howard:] Time we got at some of those weeds, 
Ben.

00:26:14.133 --> 00:26:19.799
[Dr. Ben:] Well, you know how I feel. 
I'm with you all the way, but we three alone.

00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:22.833
[Tom McAllister:] Alone! We won't be alone.

00:26:22.833 --> 00:26:25.166
Do you think we are the only people in Melton 
who want to see

00:26:25.166 --> 00:26:27.799
an end to disease and crime and poverty?

00:26:27.800 --> 00:26:30.633
Who want to uproot the weeds that infest this 
community?

00:26:30.633 --> 00:26:33.399
No.We'll find allies by the score.

00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:35.960
But let's find them. Let's get to work!

00:26:36.540 --> 00:26:38.960
[Dr. Ben:] Now you're talking.

00:26:40.900 --> 00:26:45.060
[Tom McAllister:] So we felt our first move was to 
call this meeting of representative

00:26:45.066 --> 00:26:49.966
community leaders and discover if you shared our views as I've described them to you.

00:26:49.966 --> 00:26:53.799
And if so, to enlist your support in devising a 
means of action.

00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:59.133
[Dr. Ben:] Modern medical cures are most effective, and yet the dangers are still great.

00:26:59.133 --> 00:27:03.633
The venereal disease rate in most communities far 
exceed the medical measures.

00:27:03.633 --> 00:27:08.799
We must improve our treatment service 
and our detection service.

00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:11.800
Many, many people have syphilis and do not know it.

00:27:11.800 --> 00:27:15.566
[Man 1:] Certainly we have the laws 
to combat the problem of prostitution,

00:27:15.566 --> 00:27:18.532
but we must see to it that those laws are enforced.

00:27:18.533 --> 00:27:21.666
[Marian:] And we of the Women's League 
have found time and time again

00:27:21.666 --> 00:27:27.932
that the prostitute is jailed and fined, but the man, the patron, is permitted to go free.

00:27:27.933 --> 00:27:30.833
His crime is as great as hers.

00:27:30.833 --> 00:27:35.533
[Man 2:] I feel certain industry will welcome the 
setting up of medical units to conduct

00:27:35.533 --> 00:27:40.333
general examinations, lung, x-rays and blood test 
among employees.

00:27:40.333 --> 00:27:43.666
We businessmen will cooperate 100 percent.

00:27:43.666 --> 00:27:47.299
[Dr. Ben:] Lung x-rays have uncovered a vast volume of tuberculosis,

00:27:47.300 --> 00:27:51.466
and yet little has been done to enlarge our sanatorium facilities.

00:27:51.466 --> 00:27:55.366
TB cases often have to wait their turn for 
admittance.

00:27:55.366 --> 00:27:58.199
And in the meantime the disease worsens.

00:27:58.200 --> 00:28:01.200
[Minister:] In many parts of the country, 
young people are required to have premarital

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:07.066
blood tests before they can apply for marriage licenses. Would this not be feasible in Melton?

00:28:07.066 --> 00:28:10.799
[Priest:] We of the Roman Catholic Clergy 
have very clear instructions to ask couples

00:28:10.800 --> 00:28:16.466
contemplating marriage if they have exchanged prenuptial medical certificates,

00:28:16.466 --> 00:28:20.799
and if they have not done so, we ask the reason why not.

00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:24.066
[Man 2:] What about instruction on venereal 
disease and sex knowledge in our schools?

00:28:24.066 --> 00:28:28.032
[Priest:] The knowledge first of all should be given to the parents.

00:28:28.033 --> 00:28:30.799
The adults of the community must be informed.

00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:34.566
[Man 1:] We must have civic support 
both moral and material.

00:28:34.566 --> 00:28:37.399
We need authority and money.

00:28:37.400 --> 00:28:42.633
I propose Mr. Carter, Mr. McAllister, and Dr. Edwards draw up a program for our approval

00:28:42.633 --> 00:28:46.099
summarizing and implementing our findings here 
tonight,

00:28:46.100 --> 00:28:51.366
and present that report to the city council with the very least possible delay.

00:28:51.366 --> 00:28:53.880
Let's waste no time.

00:28:56.766 --> 00:29:00.620
[Tom McAllister:] We will do our level best 
to represent adequately the

00:29:00.640 --> 00:29:03.500
splendid objectives you have set forth here 
tonight.

00:29:11.100 --> 00:29:39.560
[Daphne singing off key.]

00:29:39.566 --> 00:29:42.232
[Howard:] Daphne! Daphne!

00:29:42.233 --> 00:29:46.333
[Daphne:] Coming! Somebody call?
[Howard:] Yes, I did.

00:29:46.333 --> 00:29:49.033
That's a fine old hymn you were singing.
One of my favorites.

00:29:49.033 --> 00:29:52.966
[Daphne:] Mine too, Howard.
[Howard:] I wish you wouldn't sing it though.

00:29:52.966 --> 00:29:55.232
[Daphne:] Thought you liked it.
[Howard:] I do.

00:29:55.233 --> 00:30:00.133
And I especially like the way you sing it.
But it’s distracting.

00:30:00.133 --> 00:30:01.833
[Daphne:] 'Tis?

00:30:01.833 --> 00:30:05.633
[Howard:] Those rich full tones come floating out of 
the kitchen carrying those fine old words,

00:30:05.633 --> 00:30:10.666
I get carried away and I can't work. And I have to finish this job tonight.

00:30:10.666 --> 00:30:14.566
[Daphne:] Well, I'll just stop awhile.
Shouldn't be singing too much anyway.

00:30:14.566 --> 00:30:20.332
Might strain my voice.

00:30:20.333 --> 00:30:21.566
[Marian:] You worried about Curran?

00:30:21.566 --> 00:30:25.099
[Howard:] I know what to expect from Curran,
but Higgins...

00:30:25.100 --> 00:30:29.766
oh he's honest and means well, but not much vision.

00:30:29.766 --> 00:30:33.799
And the mayor, a straw in the wind.

00:30:33.800 --> 00:30:38.200
[Ellen:] Fifteen community leaders agreeing on a brief like this is a pretty strong wind, isn't it?

00:30:38.200 --> 00:30:42.433
[Howard:] Should be, but Curran and Higgins,
dominate the mayor.

00:30:42.433 --> 00:30:44.433
Of course, we’ll have McAllister backing us up.

00:30:44.433 --> 00:30:47.233
[Doorbell rings.]

00:30:47.233 --> 00:30:50.099
[Howard:] That must be Ben.
[Leona:] Evening, Daphne.

00:30:50.100 --> 00:30:53.866
[Charlie:] No thanks, Daphne, we just popped in for 
a minute.

00:30:53.866 --> 00:30:54.866
[Leona:] To give you the good news.
[Marian:] What news?

00:30:54.866 --> 00:30:56.799
[Leona:] We're going to be married.
[Ellen:] Leona!

00:30:56.800 --> 00:31:01.066
[Marian:] All the happiness in the world, Leona.

00:31:01.066 --> 00:31:03.466
[Howard:] Well, I hope you will be very happy.
[Charlie:] Thank you, Howard.

00:31:03.466 --> 00:31:05.966
Say where's Ben?
I thought he'd be here.

00:31:05.966 --> 00:31:08.899
[Howard:] He had to call in at the hospital, 
but he's coming.

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:10.500
[Ellen:] Why don't you wait for him?

00:31:10.500 --> 00:31:12.500
Come on Leona, come upstairs and leave your things.

00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:17.333
[Leona:] Well, we might as well stay a little while.
[Howard:] Yes, let me have your coat.

00:31:20.880 --> 00:31:23.100
[Leona:] Well, I finally nailed him.
[Ellen:] Leona.

00:31:23.100 --> 00:31:25.420
[Leona:] I'll probably regret it for the rest of my life.

00:31:25.433 --> 00:31:28.699
[Ellen:] Why do you say such things?
[Leona:] Oh, I know Charlie.

00:31:28.700 --> 00:31:31.366
He's spoiled and selfish.

00:31:31.366 --> 00:31:35.199
Marriage, it's not really what Charlie wants.

00:31:35.200 --> 00:31:40.800
The only way he could have me is to marry me,
but I haven't much in the way of values.

00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:44.833
Never was anyone to teach me anything.
Like Topsy, I just growed.

00:31:44.833 --> 00:31:48.433
Oh, Ellen, you don't know what it means not to have any family.

00:31:48.433 --> 00:31:52.199
[Ellen:] Leona, darling.
[Leona:] Ellen, I do love him.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:55.320
I hope it works out.
[Ellen:] Of course it will.

00:31:56.166 --> 00:31:58.620
[Leona:] What a goose I am.
[Ellen:] You're going to be very happy.

00:31:58.633 --> 00:32:02.933
[Leona:] I hope so.
Let’s make it a double wedding, you and Ben.

00:32:02.933 --> 00:32:05.899
[Ellen:] Leona, you idiot.
[Leona:] Now don't pretend you don't like him.

00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:10.533
[Ellen:] Of course I like him.
[Leona:] And he's just crazy about you.

00:32:10.540 --> 00:32:12.800
[Ellen:] Don't be silly.

00:32:16.566 --> 00:32:18.500
[Dr. Black:] Hello Ms. Curran.
[Patsy:] Hello, Dr. Black.

00:32:18.500 --> 00:32:21.620
[Dr. Black:] You know Dr. Edwards, I imagine.
[Patsy:] Well, what's the verdict?

00:32:21.620 --> 00:32:24.933
[Dr. Black:] Oh, sort of nerve strain, 
that's not too serious.

00:32:24.933 --> 00:32:30.533
Only a matter of too many late hours, 
too many parties, too much night life.

00:32:30.533 --> 00:32:33.766
[Patsy:] And did you have to keep me here 
for three days just to find out that?

00:32:33.766 --> 00:32:36.332
[Dr. Black:] Takes time to make a thorough 
examination.

00:32:36.333 --> 00:32:41.266
Hospitals are the best place for diagnosis.
Here we can find out exactly what's wrong.

00:32:41.266 --> 00:32:45.499
[Patsy:] But I am all right, aren't I? Well, aren't I?

00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:50.000
[Dr. Black:] I'm afraid not. Your blood test showed something quite serious.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:53.533
[Patsy:] What?
[Dr. Black:] I hate to have to tell you this.

00:32:53.533 --> 00:32:58.333
You have a venereal disease, syphilis.

00:32:58.333 --> 00:33:00.499
[Patsy:] Oh no.

00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:05.133
[Dr. Black:] You've been infected for some time.
Probably several months, but don't worry.

00:33:05.133 --> 00:33:09.233
With treatment, quite painless, 
you can be completely cured.

00:33:09.233 --> 00:33:10.699
[Patsy:] I don't believe it.

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:14.766
[Dr. Black:] I know this is a terrible shock for you,
but you'll have to face it, Miss Curran.

00:33:14.766 --> 00:33:19.066
Face not only this disease, but your own responsibility.

00:33:19.066 --> 00:33:22.132
That's why I asked Dr. Edwards to be here.
You can help him.

00:33:22.140 --> 00:33:24.200
Help him a great deal.

00:33:25.040 --> 00:33:29.333
[Dr. Ben:] Dr. Black has kindly agreed
to let me come and see you and ask your help.

00:33:29.333 --> 00:33:31.166
I hope that you ...
[Patsy:] Help with what?

00:33:31.166 --> 00:33:35.866
[Dr. Ben:] To help us trace down the source of this 
infection and what's more,

00:33:35.866 --> 00:33:38.799
help us discover any possible other infections.

00:33:38.800 --> 00:33:42.266
[Patsy:] So what do you think I am, a street walker?
[Dr. Ben:] I'm not judging you, Miss Curran.

00:33:42.266 --> 00:33:45.766
I'm a doctor with a job to do. You can help me do that job.

00:33:45.766 --> 00:33:48.199
In fact, you can be of service 
to the whole community.

00:33:48.200 --> 00:33:50.200
[Patsy:] Oh, what do I care about 
the community.

00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:52.633
Get out of here, and let me alone.
Do you understand?

00:33:52.640 --> 00:33:55.700
Get out!
Get out.

00:34:00.420 --> 00:34:05.660
Oh, oh no.

00:34:10.720 --> 00:34:13.460
[Howard:] What I have just read to you are 
the words

00:34:13.466 --> 00:34:18.199
and views of highly responsible, intelligent community leaders.

00:34:18.200 --> 00:34:22.933
As such, they deserve the respect and most searching consideration of this council.

00:34:22.933 --> 00:34:25.466
[Mr. Curran:] That all?
No specific proposals.

00:34:25.466 --> 00:34:28.199
[Howard:] Some very specific proposals.

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:33.020
But before Councilman McAllister outlines
the program recommended by our group.

00:34:33.020 --> 00:34:41.100
I want to emphasize the importance of the anti-VD phase of the program by means of a film.

00:34:41.100 --> 00:34:46.866
Dr. Edwards secured this film, and it speaks for itself most graphically.

00:34:46.866 --> 00:34:50.132
Dr. Edwards, perhaps you can set up your 
projector right now ...

00:34:50.133 --> 00:34:53.566
[Mr. Higgins:] Ah, this isn't a picture show.
Let's hear your program.

00:34:53.566 --> 00:34:55.466
[Howard:] But it only takes a few minutes.

00:34:55.466 --> 00:34:57.766
[Mr. Curran:] You've used up too much of this council's time already.

00:34:57.766 --> 00:34:59.666
Get to the point.

00:34:59.666 --> 00:35:03.232
[Mr. Mayor:] Let's view the film later.
If necessary.

00:35:03.233 --> 00:35:08.333
A most impressive report.
I'm very anxious to hear its conclusions.

00:35:08.333 --> 00:35:12.933
[Tom McAllister:] Gentlemen, here is a four-point health program for the city of Melton.

00:35:12.933 --> 00:35:17.266
It's constructed so that private citizens 
may work hand in hand with municipal departments,

00:35:17.266 --> 00:35:19.999
sharing duties and costs.

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:24.433
Point 1: Legal requirements.
A law requiring all persons

00:35:24.433 --> 00:35:28.566
to secure a general health examination, 
including blood test

00:35:28.566 --> 00:35:31.832
and lung x-ray before being issued a marriage license.

00:35:31.833 --> 00:35:36.966
New laws if necessary and intensified 
application of old laws.

00:35:36.966 --> 00:35:41.666
To prosecute not only prostitutes 
but all who derive profit therefrom:

00:35:41.666 --> 00:35:47.632
landlords, madams, pimps, and those who maintain 
prostitution by their patronage.

00:35:47.633 --> 00:35:51.733
Point 2: Medical requirements.

00:35:51.733 --> 00:35:54.333
The setting up in existing buildings of
a health center for the housing

00:35:54.333 --> 00:35:59.999
of a VD clinic, a blood test department, 
and headquarters for a mobile medical unit,

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:04.933
which would conduct general health examinations, 
lung x-rays and blood tests at the request of

00:36:04.933 --> 00:36:07.966
any individual or group of individuals.

00:36:07.966 --> 00:36:10.999
I may say gentleman, that businessmen 
among our group are especially

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:12.600
enthusiastic about this proposal.

00:36:12.600 --> 00:36:15.000
[Mr. Higgins:] Why not, something for nothing.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:19.100
[Tom McAllister:] Point 3: Citizen participation:

00:36:19.100 --> 00:36:23.333
The creation of a permanent body of 
representative citizens pledged to devise and carry

00:36:23.333 --> 00:36:29.499
out a sustained program of adult and child education on community health in all its phases.

00:36:29.500 --> 00:36:32.820
To be responsible for the raising by public subscription

00:36:32.820 --> 00:36:35.260
of one-half the cost of the community center.

00:36:35.266 --> 00:36:38.732
Point 4: Municipal participation:

00:36:38.733 --> 00:36:42.499
The city to provide the proposed health 
center referred to above.

00:36:42.500 --> 00:36:47.033
The city to provide a suitable building site 
and provide at least one-half the cost

00:36:47.033 --> 00:36:51.733
of a large community center designed to accommodate sports facilities, stage productions,

00:36:51.733 --> 00:36:56.266
public meetings, and a modest art gallery and museum.

00:36:56.266 --> 00:36:59.932
The purpose of this center being to provide a constructive environment

00:36:59.933 --> 00:37:01.799
for all the citizens of Melton.

00:37:01.800 --> 00:37:06.000
There you have it gentlemen, a first and rough plan of attack against disease

00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:07.700
and delinquency in this city.

00:37:07.700 --> 00:37:10.200
[Mr. Higgins:] What kind of wild-eyed 
nonsense is this?

00:37:10.200 --> 00:37:13.066
[Mr. Curran:] This whole plan is an insult 
to the good people of Melton.

00:37:13.066 --> 00:37:15.799
[Mr. Higgins:] An insult?
It's a fantastic slander.

00:37:15.800 --> 00:37:19.866
It suggests that Melton is a city populated by 
diseased prostitutes

00:37:19.866 --> 00:37:22.232
and degenerates, young and old.

00:37:22.233 --> 00:37:25.499
And the cost, staggering, hundreds of thousands 
of dollars.

00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:30.266
[Dr. Ben:] The cost would be a lot cheaper in the long run, than the present cost of curing disease.

00:37:30.266 --> 00:37:32.832
[Mr. Curran:] You're not a member of this council, 
Edwards.

00:37:32.833 --> 00:37:36.566
[Howard:] Gentlemen please.
[Mr. Higgins:] Are you going to have sex education
for children,

00:37:36.566 --> 00:37:39.099
expose our youngsters to stuff like that?

00:37:39.100 --> 00:37:42.566
[Tom McAllister:] I've explained that sex facts are only a part of a broad...

00:37:42.566 --> 00:37:44.799
[Mr. Higgins:] But sex would be a part.

00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:48.966
[Mr. Curran:] These blood test, x-rays, 
how many people really need them?

00:37:48.966 --> 00:37:53.332
[Mr. Higgins:] What do these fools want to do, 
stick needles in everybody in town?

00:37:53.333 --> 00:37:55.366
Treat our young people like brute cattle?

00:37:55.366 --> 00:38:01.832
[Mr. Mayor:] I feel that all these things 
could be carried out in the sanctity of the home.

00:38:01.833 --> 00:38:07.633
After all, any sensible, concerned father knows 
his duty in this regard.

00:38:07.633 --> 00:38:11.599
[Howard:] Then the fathers of this community 
are neither sensible or concerned.

00:38:11.600 --> 00:38:16.000
[Tom McAllister:] Gentlemen, we've given you
 one damaging statistic after another.

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:19.733
The alarming incidence of venereal disease, here in Melton.

00:38:19.733 --> 00:38:24.066
The consumption of alcohol by minors.
The volume of moral delinquency.

00:38:24.066 --> 00:38:27.599
The crowded sanatariums right here in this city.

00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:32.200
Can you possibly ignore these facts and bleed 
about costs and crackpots?

00:38:32.200 --> 00:38:35.700
Call the facts offensive if you wish, but as representatives

00:38:35.700 --> 00:38:38.533
of the people you dare not turn your backs on them.

00:38:38.533 --> 00:38:40.666
Nor on the need for a program of action.

00:38:40.666 --> 00:38:43.666
[Mr. Curran:] Perhaps we let this idea take us by 
surprise.

00:38:43.666 --> 00:38:45.299
Let's study it.

00:38:45.300 --> 00:38:49.300
I move that a committee of three be appointed
to investigate and report back to the council.

00:38:49.300 --> 00:38:51.400
[Tom McAllister:] I second that motion.
[Mr. Higgins:] I nominate Curran.

00:38:51.400 --> 00:38:52.766
[Tom McAllister:] Carter.

00:38:52.766 --> 00:38:55.532
[Curran:] This is a mighty important committee.
I think the mayor should be on there.

00:38:55.533 --> 00:38:59.433
[Mr. Mayor:] I'd be delighted, gentlemen.
It is an important committee.

00:38:59.433 --> 00:39:01.399
[Mr. Higgins:] Well you got three, now let it go at 
that.

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:05.566
[Mr. Mayor:] Is that your wish, gentlemen?
[Mr. Higgins:] Anyway, I move we adjourn.

00:39:05.566 --> 00:39:08.232
[Mr. Curran:] Second it.
[Howard:] The film, you should see the film.

00:39:08.233 --> 00:39:10.366
[Mr. Higgins:] Let the committee see the film.
[Mr. Mayor:] When do we meet?

00:39:10.366 --> 00:39:15.766
[Mr. Curran:] I'll call you.
[Dr. Ben:] Well, at least we got a committee.

00:39:15.766 --> 00:39:18.799
[Mr. Howard:] Yes, we go through a farce of 
meetings.

00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:22.366
[Tom McAllister:] And Curran will try to talk the plan 
to death, an old strategy of his.

00:39:22.366 --> 00:39:25.332
There will be a whispering campaign, opposition generated.

00:39:25.333 --> 00:39:31.299
If we ever get to the public with this idea they'll be so influenced against...oh well.

00:39:31.300 --> 00:39:33.933
[Mr. Howard:] The public. Mac, that’s it.

00:39:33.933 --> 00:39:38.833
We won't wait for Curran to get in his dirty work.
We'll take this idea to the people themselves.

00:39:38.833 --> 00:39:41.133
[Tom McAllister:] The annual town meeting?
[Mr. Howard:] Exactly!

00:39:41.133 --> 00:39:45.099
But we'll have that meeting primed:
speeches, leaflets, polls.

00:39:45.100 --> 00:39:49.266
We'll start a publicity campaign between now and the meeting.

00:39:49.266 --> 00:39:51.232
[Dr. Ben:] Hey, what meeting, what’s that?

00:39:51.233 --> 00:39:54.466
[Tom McAllister:] Once a year the council meets 
in the presence of the public, an old custom here.

00:39:54.466 --> 00:39:59.399
[Mr. Howard:] Ben, my boy, as somebody said somewhere, we've only just begun to fight.

00:39:59.400 --> 00:40:04.360
[Newspaper presses running.]

00:40:04.360 --> 00:41:02.500
[Dramatic music playing as newspaper headlines are displayed.]

00:41:02.500 --> 00:41:04.366
[Dr. Ben:] Look, even the decent newspapers are against us.

00:41:04.366 --> 00:41:06.999
[Ellen:] I can't understand it, why?

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:10.733
[Dr. Ben:] Ahhh, I guess it’s so easy 
to stir up prejudice and fear.

00:41:10.733 --> 00:41:12.333
[Ellen:] Poor dad.

00:41:12.333 --> 00:41:14.466
He's worried sick, blames himself over what's 
happening.

00:41:14.466 --> 00:41:18.666
[Dr. Ben:] It's not his fault.
Curran and his tribe distorted everything.

00:41:18.666 --> 00:41:24.066
[Ellen:] Well, we just have to keep on fighting.
[Dr. Ben:] You're a tower of strength. Ellen?

00:41:24.066 --> 00:41:27.299
[Charlie:] Hi folks, am I breaking something up. I'll bet!

00:41:27.300 --> 00:41:29.633
[Ellen:] Hello, Charlie.
[Charlie:] You ready to go Ben?

00:41:29.633 --> 00:41:31.133
[Dr. Ben:] Ready?

00:41:31.133 --> 00:41:33.833
[Charlie:] Up north to the ski lodge,
to help fix up for the honeymooners?

00:41:33.833 --> 00:41:36.833
[Dr. Ben:] Awww, I've been so busy Charlie,
I guess I forgot.

00:41:36.833 --> 00:41:38.399
I don't think I'll be able to make it.

00:41:38.400 --> 00:41:40.666
[Charlie:] You haven't a single appointment, I just 
checked.

00:41:40.666 --> 00:41:43.166
[Ellen:] Why don't you go, Ben?
The drive will do you good.

00:41:43.166 --> 00:41:44.532
[Dr. Ben:] Will you come?

00:41:44.533 --> 00:41:48.466
[Ellen:] I can't really, but you go please.
[Dr. Ben:] Okay.

00:41:48.466 --> 00:41:52.199
[Charlie:] Ellen you have him well-trained.
I bow to you, my pet.

00:41:52.200 --> 00:41:54.733
[Ellen chuckles.]

00:41:54.733 --> 00:42:09.566
[Music playing.]

00:42:09.566 --> 00:42:12.699
[Charlie:] Leona can have her flowers, 
I'll take pine needles. Here grab some of that.

00:42:12.700 --> 00:42:14.533
[Dr. Ben:] Yeah, yeah.

00:42:14.533 --> 00:42:17.799
[Charlie:] My little wife-to-be will probably 
chuck this stuff out once she sees it.

00:42:17.800 --> 00:42:21.633
Women hate to have things arranged for them. 
Like to do it themselves.

00:42:21.633 --> 00:42:26.966
You'll find that out soon enough, Ben, if you ever 
stop chasing germs and start chasing women.

00:42:26.966 --> 00:42:28.799
Well, I guess my chasing days are over.

00:42:28.800 --> 00:42:30.733
[Dr. Ben:] Well, they should be.

00:42:30.733 --> 00:42:33.666
You've chased and caught a very lovely girl. 
See that you deserve her.

00:42:33.666 --> 00:42:36.232
[Charlie:] Yes, doctor.
Say, the place looks good, eh?

00:42:36.233 --> 00:42:41.166
[Dr. Ben:] Neat as a pen.
What's this?

00:42:41.166 --> 00:42:45.060
[Charlie:] Oh, some trinket of Leona's.
I'll take that.

00:42:45.060 --> 00:42:50.120
[Patsy Curran is engraved on the bracelet.]

00:42:52.600 --> 00:42:54.600
An ancient indiscretion.

00:42:54.600 --> 00:42:58.500
[Dr. Ben:] How ancient?
[Charlie:] Chap doesn't discuss these things.

00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:00.340
[Dr. Ben:] He does with his doctor.

00:43:03.066 --> 00:43:06.500
[Charlie:] A few weeks ago.
[Dr. Ben:] When Leona was in the city?

00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:08.566
Very ancient.

00:43:08.566 --> 00:43:11.766
[Charlie:] Hang it all, Ben.
Stop talking like a made man.

00:43:11.766 --> 00:43:13.766
What business is it of yours anyway?

00:43:13.766 --> 00:43:17.160
[Dr. Ben:] Come on, we're going back to my office.

00:43:17.160 --> 00:43:20.500
[Charlie:] Honestly Ben, this is a lot of rot.

00:43:20.500 --> 00:43:24.166
All right, give me your old blood test,
but don't interfere in my private life.

00:43:24.166 --> 00:43:27.899
[Dr. Ben:] I've told you it takes time 
for us doctors to make sure.

00:43:27.900 --> 00:43:30.300
If you are going to be a silly young fool running 
around,

00:43:30.300 --> 00:43:33.566
you owe it to your future wife to make absolutely 
certain.

00:43:33.566 --> 00:43:35.299
You can't get married until you are.

00:43:35.300 --> 00:43:39.833
[Charlie:] How long is that?
[Dr. Ben:] Might take ten weeks or even longer.

00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:45.100
[Charlie:] Postpone the marriage indefinitely.
I should say not.

00:43:45.200 --> 00:43:46.420
[Dr. Ben:] Silly young fool.

00:43:48.600 --> 00:43:52.020
[Charlie:] There are these new drugs, even if 
anything were wrong.

00:43:56.480 --> 00:43:58.040
[Dr. Ben:] 391

00:44:05.460 --> 00:44:08.620
[Patsy:] Hello.
[Dr. Ben:] Hello Miss Curran, this is Dr. Edwards.

00:44:08.633 --> 00:44:09.866
[Patsy:] Yes.

00:44:09.866 --> 00:44:12.366
[Dr. Ben:] I'd like for you to come over to my office 
immediately.

00:44:12.366 --> 00:44:15.099
[Patsy:] Well look, Dr. Edwards, I've got absolutely nothing to talk to you about.

00:44:15.100 --> 00:44:20.166
[Dr. Ben:] I have Charlie Mitchell here, and your bracelet.

00:44:20.166 --> 00:44:24.732
[Patsy:] Oh, all right.
As soon as I can.

00:44:24.740 --> 00:44:29.160
[Dr. Ben:] Goodbye.
Better sit down.

00:44:31.400 --> 00:44:45.900
[Men are gathered around a meeting table.]

00:44:45.900 --> 00:44:47.066
[Mr. Curran:] Thought I told you not to come up 
here.

00:44:47.066 --> 00:44:48.966
[Shorty:] I've got something very important, boss.

00:44:48.966 --> 00:44:51.999
[Mr. Mayor:] Good government, Higgins, is cautious 
government.

00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:55.066
Go slowly. Be sure, be patient.

00:44:55.066 --> 00:44:58.466
[Mr. Higgins:] Patience and caution, go slowly and 
solidly.

00:44:58.466 --> 00:45:00.180
[Mr. Mayor:] Yes, exactly.

00:45:03.700 --> 00:45:04.600
[Mr. Curran:] Listen to this, Mitchell.

00:45:04.600 --> 00:45:08.800
[Shorty:] I'm downstairs see, waiting for you, boss, 
when in through a side door comes Patsy.

00:45:08.800 --> 00:45:12.133
"What she doing here," I think?
I follow her down the corridor to the back.

00:45:12.133 --> 00:45:15.266
She goes into Edwards' office.
I'm surprised, you get me.

00:45:15.266 --> 00:45:17.099
We don't go for this Edwards guy, do we boss?
What's Patsy doing...

00:45:17.100 --> 00:45:18.733
[Mr. Curran:] Never mind that.

00:45:18.733 --> 00:45:20.266
[Shorty:] Well, I'm curious, see.

00:45:20.266 --> 00:45:26.232
So I tippy-toe into the other room, empty, 
but in the other office I hear voices.

00:45:26.233 --> 00:45:30.899
Edwards, Patsy, and your kid mayor. 
[Mr. Mayor:] Charlie?

00:45:30.900 --> 00:45:32.000
[Shorty:] The same.

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:35.400
[Mr. Curran:] This guy Edwards is up to something.
Come on Mitchell.

00:45:35.400 --> 00:45:37.666
[Charlie:] Look Ben, will you get to the point, 
whatever it is?

00:45:37.666 --> 00:45:40.932
[Patsy:] Yeah, what do you want anyway?
[Dr. Ben:] I want you to tell Charlie the truth.

00:45:40.933 --> 00:45:45.566
[Charlie:] What do you mean?
[Patsy:] Well, you're not tongue-tied?

00:45:45.566 --> 00:45:48.666
You had to drag me down here for that.
[Dr. Ben:] You're the only one to speak.

00:45:48.666 --> 00:45:51.666
It's your duty. I don't seem to be able to convince you of that.

00:45:51.666 --> 00:45:56.032
[Patsy:] You're not going to pry into my life.
[Charlie:] Look, will you get to the point?

00:45:56.033 --> 00:46:01.666
[Dr. Ben:] Very well. I'm going to show 
you something and after you've seen it,

00:46:01.666 --> 00:46:06.199
perhaps you'll come over to my point of view,
and realize how important it is

00:46:06.200 --> 00:46:08.200
for both of you to cooperate with me.

00:46:10.360 --> 00:46:13.120
[Charlie:] What's the meaning of this?
[Mr. Curran:] Never mind that.

00:46:13.133 --> 00:46:15.599
What's he got on you two?

00:46:15.600 --> 00:46:18.166
[Dr. Ben:] Curran, this is a doctor's office.
What goes on in here is secret.

00:46:18.166 --> 00:46:19.732
[Mr. Curran:] I wonder.

00:46:19.733 --> 00:46:25.066
You might be digging for dirt against our two kids
in order to force Mitchell and me to back your lousy health campaign.

00:46:25.066 --> 00:46:26.599
To make a big name for yourself.

00:46:26.600 --> 00:46:30.566
[Dr. Ben:] You might have told your family 
as your doctor instructed you to.

00:46:30.566 --> 00:46:34.800
[Mr. Curran:] Told what? Answer me, what's he talking about?

00:46:34.960 --> 00:46:36.740
[Patsy:] Oh, leave me alone.

00:46:38.080 --> 00:46:41.160
[Charlie:] Ben, you mean there is really something 
wrong?

00:46:41.160 --> 00:46:44.560
[Mr. Curran:] Patsy, tell me.

00:46:48.120 --> 00:46:52.740
[Patsy:] Well, if you must know, I've got syphilis.

00:46:53.000 --> 00:47:03.560
[Dramatic music.]

00:47:05.020 --> 00:47:06.140
[Mr. Mayor:] Charlie?

00:47:12.940 --> 00:47:17.633
[Charlie:] I guess I maybe...

00:47:17.633 --> 00:47:23.299
[Dr. Ben:] I asked Patsy and Charlie here together so they could see what might happen to them.

00:47:23.300 --> 00:47:27.500
It's doubtful that it will happen, thanks to science, but it could happen.

00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:30.900
I think it’s most appropriate that you two gentlemen 
dropped in.

00:47:30.900 --> 00:47:35.260
You need to see these films I have here
as much as your children do.

00:47:43.060 --> 00:47:44.100
Sit down gentlemen.

00:47:44.100 --> 00:48:15.360
[Sounds of projector being set up, and music as film opens]

00:48:15.366 --> 00:48:19.832
[Narrator:] Syphilis the crippler, 
the destroyer, the killer.

00:48:19.833 --> 00:48:24.266
Usually contracted sooner or later by men 
associating with prostitutes

00:48:24.266 --> 00:48:27.460
or indulging in promiscuous sex relationships.

00:48:28.320 --> 00:48:32.533
So often acquired by girls who foolishly become sexually intimate

00:48:32.533 --> 00:48:37.366
with men they meet as dance hall pickups.
Or at the drinking parties.

00:48:37.366 --> 00:48:43.200
And the story of Jerry Anderson again and again.

00:48:45.380 --> 00:48:48.633
[Doctor 1:] What's your name?
[Jerry Anderson:] Jerry Anderson.

00:48:48.633 --> 00:48:52.933
[Doctor 1:] Jerry Anderson.
How did you happen to come into the clinic?

00:48:52.933 --> 00:48:55.933
[Jerry Anderson:] Well, I couldn't afford to 
go to a private doctor.

00:48:55.933 --> 00:48:58.266
I didn't know what to do.

00:48:58.266 --> 00:49:01.732
I called the county health department to see 
if they couldn't do something for me.

00:49:01.733 --> 00:49:03.466
I was told to come see you.

00:49:03.466 --> 00:49:06.032
[Doctor 1:] What's your trouble, Jerry?

00:49:06.033 --> 00:49:09.799
[Jerry Anderson:] Well, I've got a pretty bad sore 
down here.

00:49:09.800 --> 00:49:11.433
[Doctor 1:] Umhmm.

00:49:11.440 --> 00:49:15.080
Why don't you stretch out on that table over there? 
We'll have a look at you.

00:49:18.580 --> 00:49:20.720
Come over here.

00:49:20.720 --> 00:49:25.460
I want you to see this little cork screw devil
that's causing all your trouble.

00:49:25.460 --> 00:49:26.500
Look.

00:49:32.900 --> 00:49:36.260
This darkfield test shows up the spirochetes.

00:49:36.266 --> 00:49:39.532
Can you see them wriggling back and forth across 
the slide?

00:49:39.533 --> 00:49:43.466
[Jerry Anderson:] Yes, what did you call them?
[Doctor 1:] Spirochetes.

00:49:43.466 --> 00:49:46.180
Those are the germs that cause your syphilis.

00:49:52.466 --> 00:49:54.120
[Jerry Anderson:] Well, I guess that finishes me.

00:49:54.133 --> 00:49:59.533
I'll have to leave home, quit school, and go 
someplace where people don't know who I am.

00:49:59.533 --> 00:50:03.699
[Doctor 1:] Now Jerry, you know can't meet any problem by running away from it.

00:50:03.700 --> 00:50:06.066
You may not realize it, but you're a very lucky young man,

00:50:06.066 --> 00:50:08.866
because we're catching this in time to cure you.

00:50:08.866 --> 00:50:11.520
Ms. Jones, prepare a 4/10ths neo-injection, please.

00:50:11.640 --> 00:50:13.720
[Jerry Anderson:] Yes, but doctor I can't take a chance on the folks

00:50:13.720 --> 00:50:15.760
or their kids at school finding out that I have 
syphilis.

00:50:15.760 --> 00:50:17.380
[Doctor 1:] Now don't worry about it.

00:50:18.966 --> 00:50:22.660
You can go about your class work, play basketball, 
tennis, or indulge in any other sport.

00:50:22.666 --> 00:50:25.099
Sit down here please and roll up your sleeve.

00:50:25.100 --> 00:50:28.266
And nobody need ever know that you have 
syphilis.

00:50:28.266 --> 00:50:33.766
But you have to report every week, and not miss a 
single treatment at least for one year.

00:50:33.766 --> 00:50:37.640
[Jerry Anderson:] Well, that's a relief.
I feel like living again.

00:50:48.900 --> 00:50:51.160
Gee doctor, that didn't hurt a bit.

00:50:51.166 --> 00:50:53.199
I'd always heard that shots for syphilis were 
painful.

00:50:53.200 --> 00:50:56.533
[Doctor 1:] Not if you go to a doctor who knows his 
business.

00:50:56.533 --> 00:50:58.299
[Jerry Anderson:] I don't know how to thank you, 
doctor.

00:50:58.300 --> 00:51:01.700
[Doctor 1:] Just come into my office, and give me 
the name of the girl that infected you.

00:51:01.700 --> 00:51:04.260
That's all the thanks I want.
Come along.

00:51:07.266 --> 00:51:09.220
[Jerry Anderson:] Gee doctor, I kinda hate to do 
that.

00:51:09.233 --> 00:51:11.099
I'm no stool pigeon.

00:51:11.100 --> 00:51:13.666
[Doctor 1:] Sit down here, please.

00:51:13.666 --> 00:51:17.066
Now Jerry a lot of men have a false sense of 
chivalry about giving the name of the

00:51:17.066 --> 00:51:19.032
woman that infected them.

00:51:19.033 --> 00:51:24.499
We're not going to do anything harmful to the girl,
and your name won't be brought into it.

00:51:24.500 --> 00:51:29.033
We only want to bring her in for examination and 
treatment.

00:51:29.033 --> 00:51:30.866
[Narrator:] Jerry has done his part.

00:51:30.866 --> 00:51:34.499
Now the health department swings into action to do theirs.

00:51:34.500 --> 00:51:39.700
This health official studying the information on 
the card sent into the department by the doctor

00:51:39.700 --> 00:51:45.600
who examined Jerry Anderson rings for a visiting 
health nurse.

00:51:45.600 --> 00:51:50.300
After discussing the case for a few moments,
the nurse sets out to locate the girl,

00:51:50.300 --> 00:51:56.166
and, in a friendly way and confidential interview,
suggests that the girl visit the clinic

00:51:56.166 --> 00:51:59.900
in the interest of her own health and welfare.

00:52:04.500 --> 00:52:10.033
Upon reporting to the clinic for an examination and 
interview, a sample of the girl's blood is taken

00:52:10.033 --> 00:52:13.899
and sent to the departmental laboratory for 
analysis.

00:52:13.900 --> 00:52:18.866
This contact or suspected contact follow-up 
procedure is very important to the individual

00:52:18.866 --> 00:52:26.232
concerned because so often they do not even 
suspect they are suffering from venereal disease.

00:52:26.233 --> 00:52:30.599
The laboratory examination of the blood sample,
generally known as the Wasserman test,

00:52:30.600 --> 00:52:35.266
is a complicated procedure requiring close 
attention to detail.

00:52:35.266 --> 00:52:39.099
It is entrusted only to thoroughly skilled personnel
who handle these tests quickly

00:52:39.100 --> 00:52:41.300
and efficiently by number.

00:52:41.300 --> 00:52:44.500
They never know the name of the patient involved.

00:52:44.500 --> 00:52:48.100
In this instance, the test confirmed 
that Jerry's sex partner had syphilis.

00:52:48.100 --> 00:52:52.660
There is no doubt of it.
The laboratory report is positive.

00:52:58.180 --> 00:53:07.300
Syphilis has struck and its germs are implanted 
in new victims once again.

00:53:07.300 --> 00:53:12.300
Just a little over three weeks since Jerry met the girl who infected him with syphilis,

00:53:12.300 --> 00:53:16.740
which began in her case most probably through intercourse with an infected person

00:53:16.740 --> 00:53:19.360
prior to her relations with Jerry Anderson.

00:53:19.366 --> 00:53:23.666
Now we see what really happens in such a case 
as the germs of syphilis, called spirochetes,

00:53:23.666 --> 00:53:28.700
attack the cervix or neck of the uterus 
within the female reproductive system.

00:53:29.320 --> 00:53:34.833
Shortly after infection, the primary lesions,
or chancres as they are commonly called,

00:53:34.833 --> 00:53:40.566
appear as small, red sores where the spirochetes entered the bloodstream.

00:53:40.566 --> 00:53:48.580
Such as the labia, or lips of the vulva, 
on the vaginal wall, and the cervix.

00:53:49.080 --> 00:53:53.400
Since these sores are painless 
and often well concealed within the female organs,

00:53:53.400 --> 00:53:58.766
it is easy to understand why women in particular 
can be infected and never know it.

00:53:58.766 --> 00:54:03.999
Syphilis can also, in very rare cases, be acquired 
by kissing a person with a chancre on the lips,

00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:08.240
and occasionally doctors and nurses contract it
in handling syphilitic patients,

00:54:08.240 --> 00:54:11.680
in which event the chancres appear on the finger like this.

00:54:12.940 --> 00:54:17.520
Throughout the primary stage and during the quiescent period of from six weeks to three months

00:54:17.520 --> 00:54:22.000
following the appearance of the chancres, 
the germs are disseminated to all parts

00:54:22.000 --> 00:54:24.400
of the body via the bloodstream,

00:54:24.400 --> 00:54:29.366
their natural highway network reaching 
to every vital organ of the human system.

00:54:29.366 --> 00:54:33.666
The disease now enters upon what is known as the 
secondary stage,

00:54:33.666 --> 00:54:39.499
and various manifestations may begin to appear, either singly or in combination.

00:54:39.500 --> 00:54:41.000
Such as headaches.

00:54:41.000 --> 00:54:46.700
Accompanied by general feeling of depression 
of being unwell, with perhaps sores in the mouth,

00:54:46.700 --> 00:54:49.880
sore throat, or swollen glands.

00:54:50.640 --> 00:54:55.566
The infected bloodstream may give rise 
to skin rashes on the body and face.

00:54:55.566 --> 00:55:01.566
Or the hair roots may be affected and unsightly 
patches appear at different places.

00:55:01.566 --> 00:55:11.166
Or as so often happens, a general falling of the hair during combing, from all parts of the scalp.

00:55:11.166 --> 00:55:14.632
Health authorities have ascertained
by careful checking of their records,

00:55:14.633 --> 00:55:18.433
that one case of syphilis usually results in three 
more.

00:55:18.440 --> 00:55:23.900
And those three, another three.
Therefore it is your duty, yours and mine,

00:55:23.900 --> 00:55:30.460
should any of these manifestations appear,
such as headaches, sores in the mouth,

00:55:30.466 --> 00:55:36.066
sore throat, swollen glands, skin rashes, hair patches, etc., especially after exposure

00:55:36.066 --> 00:55:43.632
through illicit sex relations, to report to a private physician or health clinic for examination and a blood test.

00:55:43.640 --> 00:55:48.700
Which is simplicity itself, and when carried out by a skilled operator,

00:55:48.700 --> 00:55:51.833
is so painless as to be almost unnoticeable.

00:55:51.833 --> 00:55:56.466
A tourniquet is first applied to the arm,
which is then thoroughly cleansed with alcohol.

00:55:56.466 --> 00:56:01.532
A large syringe is now deftly inserted into a vein 
and a quantity of blood

00:56:01.533 --> 00:56:07.233
slowly withdrawn for laboratory analysis purposes.
And that’s all there is to it.

00:56:07.240 --> 00:56:08.720
Bets.

00:56:08.800 --> 00:56:13.900
The beneficial results may be far reaching 
and save untold misery

00:56:13.900 --> 00:56:16.966
and unnecessary suffering in later years.

00:56:16.966 --> 00:56:20.732
If in doubt at anytime don't delay, 
get a blood test today.

00:56:20.740 --> 00:56:26.960
Your own health and the health of your loved ones
is far too precious to gamble away.

00:56:28.300 --> 00:56:32.300
Time is the all-important factor 
in the war on syphilis.

00:56:32.520 --> 00:56:36.120
Prompt treatment by a qualified physician
or at a health clinic is insurance

00:56:36.120 --> 00:56:39.960
against the devastating effects of late syphilis.

00:56:39.966 --> 00:56:44.766
Which may appear anywhere from five to ten, 
fifteen, or even twenty years

00:56:44.766 --> 00:56:46.899
after the original infection,

00:56:46.900 --> 00:56:52.420
If the disease is not detected and treated in the early stages.

00:56:53.566 --> 00:56:58.820
The heart attack, the usual cardiac symptoms,
associated with heart trouble--

00:56:58.833 --> 00:57:02.966
in reality syphilis in disguise--
because syphilis will simulate

00:57:02.966 --> 00:57:07.399
practically every disease known to medical science.

00:57:07.400 --> 00:57:12.033
Stricken without warning, 
from the very depths of our being.

00:57:12.033 --> 00:57:20.666
Even death, yes, is often the penalty paid 
for neglect of this scourge of the human race.

00:57:20.666 --> 00:57:24.832
When the spirochetes attack the optic nerve, 
blindness can be

00:57:24.833 --> 00:57:28.566
the tragic aftermath of this fearful disease.

00:57:28.566 --> 00:57:34.066
If and when they invade the central nervous system, locomotor ataxia,

00:57:34.066 --> 00:57:39.132
paralysis of the lower limbs, often occurs.

00:57:39.133 --> 00:57:43.833
But when they attack the brain,
then we pay the terrible price of paresis

00:57:43.840 --> 00:57:50.660
with the pitiable hallucinations, gradual loss of 
speech, eventual mental unbalance, and death.

00:57:50.660 --> 00:57:55.260
Tragic human wrecks on the casualty list of the 
great destroyer.

00:57:55.266 --> 00:57:56.866
[Man babbling]

00:57:56.866 --> 00:57:59.999
[Interviewer:] Tell me how is your memory?
[Man Interviewed:] Memory 100 percent?

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.000
[Continued babbling "God bless you, Happy New 
Year"]

00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:03.900
[Interviewer:] How are your spirits? 
[Man Interviewed:] Spirits 100 percent.

00:58:03.900 --> 00:58:10.266
[Interviewer:]Are you happy? You're happy?
[Man babbling]

00:58:10.266 --> 00:58:14.332
[Interviewer:] I want you to say this after me, 
lovely, lily, lemon.

00:58:14.333 --> 00:58:17.199
[Man interviewed:] Lovely, lily, lemon.
[Interviewer:] Lovely, lily, lemon.

00:58:17.200 --> 00:58:19.366
[Man interviewed:] One hundred percent.
[Interviewer:] Truly rural.

00:58:19.366 --> 00:58:22.366
[Man interviewed:] Truly lurul.
 [Interviewer:] Truly rural.

00:58:22.366 --> 00:58:23.966
[Man interviewed:] Truly tlulul.

00:58:23.966 --> 00:58:27.360
[Interviewer:] Liquid electricity.
[Man interviewed:] Liquid ectricity.

00:58:28.540 --> 00:58:33.100
[Narrator:]  In these late cases of syphilis, 
the spinal tap is often the only means

00:58:33.100 --> 00:58:37.066
of determining the true cause of the patient's 
condition.

00:58:37.066 --> 00:58:41.266
Like the blood test we saw earlier,
the technique involves insertion of a needle,

00:58:41.266 --> 00:58:45.466
only this time a hollow one into the spinal canal.

00:58:45.466 --> 00:58:49.066
And the spinal fluid for the laboratory analysis is caught in test tubes

00:58:49.066 --> 00:58:52.232
as it drips through the hollow needle from the spinal column.

00:58:52.233 --> 00:58:57.733
Today in view of all that is known about syphilis, many physicians take a spinal as an extra measure

00:58:57.733 --> 00:59:01.833
of precaution in all cases of patients receiving 
antisyphilitic treatment

00:59:01.840 --> 00:59:04.680
before discharging them as completely cured.

00:59:06.840 --> 00:59:09.660
[Butcher painting store window]

00:59:09.660 --> 00:59:47.300
[Inaudible talking]

00:59:47.300 --> 01:00:01.660
[Ambulance arrives]

01:00:03.040 --> 01:00:04.980
[Butcher Tony:] I got everything all ready doctor.

01:00:08.300 --> 01:00:12.060
My wife she’s in this room, and she got her sister with her too.

01:00:12.060 --> 01:00:17.340
Please doctor, hurry up, huh. I'll stay right here, waiting for the good news.

01:00:23.440 --> 01:00:30.166
What you want let me get on and finish in peace.
Outside. [Inaudible]

01:00:30.166 --> 01:00:37.280
Thank you, everybody.

01:00:44.966 --> 01:01:54.160
[The doctor delivers the baby.]

01:01:54.166 --> 01:02:08.132
[Butcher playing accordion as he waits.]

01:02:08.133 --> 01:02:11.266
[Butcher Tony:] What's a matter doc?
Don't you want to tell me she's a boy?

01:02:11.266 --> 01:02:13.699
He's a boy, no?

01:02:13.700 --> 01:02:17.466
[Doctor:] Yes Tony, it's a boy.
[Butcher Toni:] My Maria, Maria, she's okay?

01:02:17.466 --> 01:02:18.966
[Doctor:] She's all right.

01:02:18.966 --> 01:02:25.399
[Butcher Tony:] My bambino's all right, my Maria's all right, but your face isn't all right.

01:02:25.400 --> 01:02:27.800
What's the matter?

01:02:29.420 --> 01:02:35.680
[Doctor:] Tony, your son was born dead.
[Tony drops the accordion.]

01:02:39.960 --> 01:02:44.020
[Butcher Toni:] My first bambino is dead. 
What's that?

01:02:44.033 --> 01:02:48.166
[Doctor:] Well, I've got a pretty good idea,
But I’ll have to ask you a few questions first.

01:02:48.166 --> 01:02:51.732
[Butcher Tony:] Questions, what questions?

01:02:51.733 --> 01:02:53.733
[Doctor:] We’re not done Tony, I better wait until your wife feels better.

01:02:53.733 --> 01:02:56.033
[Butcher Tony:] Oh please, now you’re driving me crazy. What's happened?

01:02:56.040 --> 01:02:58.220
[Doctor:] All right.

01:03:00.020 --> 01:03:02.660
Did anyone ever tell you Tony, that you've got syphilis?

01:03:02.666 --> 01:03:05.599
[Butcher Tony:] Syphil... What are you talking about? I ain't got no syphilis.

01:03:05.600 --> 01:03:08.860
[Doctor:] Take it easy. Think, I want you to think 
back carefully.

01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:14.433
Do you remember ever having a sore 
that didn't heal very fast?

01:03:14.433 --> 01:03:17.633
[Butcher Tony:] No, no I never...

01:03:17.633 --> 01:03:21.599
Yes, about two years ago, before I was married.

01:03:21.600 --> 01:03:26.133
I got a little sore, but I got a salve and put it on it 
and it was cured.

01:03:26.140 --> 01:03:30.120
[Doctor:] It might make the sore go away, but no medicine you could buy ever cured syphilis.

01:03:32.540 --> 01:03:34.233
[Butcher Tony:] I got syphilis?

01:03:34.233 --> 01:03:36.999
[Doctor:] I'm almost sure syphilis killed your baby, Tony.

01:03:37.000 --> 01:03:44.566
You see, a syphilitic sore will go away without any treatment in time, but the germs stay in your body.

01:03:44.566 --> 01:03:50.300
[Doctor:] Yes Tony, I'm afraid that you gave Maria syphilis, and she gave it to the baby.

01:03:56.366 --> 01:04:01.400
[Narrator:] Sins of the father visit upon such 
babies, and these children born deformed,

01:04:01.400 --> 01:04:06.400
unsightly and handicapped throughout their life.

01:04:06.400 --> 01:04:11.860
Or like this little boy with the doctor,
deaf for the rest of his life.

01:04:17.140 --> 01:04:22.960
Venereal disease can be cured.

01:04:27.280 --> 01:04:29.420
Thanks to medical science.

01:04:30.740 --> 01:04:34.340
And particularly syphilis can be completely stamped out,

01:04:35.340 --> 01:04:40.280
if all engaged couples went to a doctor for a premarital consultation,

01:04:40.280 --> 01:04:47.340
a thorough physical examination before marriage, and a routine blood test.

01:04:48.040 --> 01:04:54.380
If every expectant mother made certain that she received adequate prenatal care,

01:04:54.380 --> 01:05:04.220
including the routine blood test early in pregnancy, then congenital syphilis could be stamped out.

01:05:05.220 --> 01:05:11.800
If we demanded and supported routine blood tests 
for employees in every industry,

01:05:12.500 --> 01:05:20.133
if we demanded and supported adult classes of instruction in sex education.

01:05:20.133 --> 01:05:27.633
And if we all, whenever our own status was in doubt, reported to a private physician

01:05:27.633 --> 01:05:37.033
or a health clinic and asked for a blood test, then indeed the day would come when everyone would

01:05:37.040 --> 01:05:42.480
know for sure, and syphilis would become a disease of the past within the very near future.

01:05:45.940 --> 01:05:56.180
[Dr. Ben, Pasy, Charlie, and their fathers are sitting in the doctor's office.]

01:05:56.180 --> 01:05:59.520
[Dr. Ben:] That is what I tried to show at the council 
meeting the other night.

01:05:59.520 --> 01:06:03.060
That is part of what the four-point program is aimed against.

01:06:03.066 --> 01:06:05.399
That's all gentlemen.

01:06:05.400 --> 01:06:10.060
[Charlie:] Ben? It will be all right? In time?

01:06:10.060 --> 01:06:12.733
[Dr. Ben:] Yes. We can cure this disease.

01:06:12.733 --> 01:06:16.733
We can cure the body that is,
but the spirit is something else.

01:06:16.733 --> 01:06:20.433
It might bear permanent scars.
That's up to you.

01:06:20.440 --> 01:06:23.766
[Charlie:] Thanks Ben.
And we'll do whatever you say.

01:06:25.640 --> 01:06:28.800
[Patsy:] May I go now?
[Dr. Ben:] Yes.

01:06:28.800 --> 01:06:30.700
It will be all right Patsy, don't worry.

01:06:33.380 --> 01:06:41.860
[Mr. Curran:] Patsy! It's all my fault, baby.
[Patsy:] Oh dad!

01:06:42.400 --> 01:06:46.800
[Dr. Ben:] Let me repeat, Curran.
All this is between the five of us.

01:06:52.960 --> 01:06:55.960
[Mr. Mayor:] You mean that this won't get out?
No one will know?

01:06:55.966 --> 01:06:58.132
[Dr. Ben:] I think I made that quite clear, Mr. Mayor.

01:06:58.133 --> 01:07:01.666
[Mr. Mayor:] Yes, but the wedding will have 
to be postponed, and people do...

01:07:01.666 --> 01:07:03.732
Then there's the health program?

01:07:03.733 --> 01:07:08.166
[Dr. Ben:] Our differences are not political ones.
We are not fighting for power, for votes.

01:07:08.166 --> 01:07:12.500
We're fighting disease, stunted minds, and stunted 
bodies.

01:07:13.960 --> 01:07:15.140
[Charlie:] Come on, dad.

01:07:15.480 --> 01:07:21.760
[Dramatic music.]

01:07:21.760 --> 01:07:26.880
[Charlie:] Well, that's it.
[Leona:] What do you have to do?

01:07:26.880 --> 01:07:28.533
[Charlie:] Well, I'll move to the city.

01:07:28.540 --> 01:07:32.980
Father's fixed up a job for me, and Ben has 
arranged for treatments there.

01:07:32.980 --> 01:07:37.533
It'll, it'll look quite normal to postpone the wedding.

01:07:37.533 --> 01:07:43.666
[Leona:] Postpone it?
[Charlie:] Leona, are you through with me?

01:07:43.666 --> 01:07:48.699
[Leona:] No. No, I love you Charlie.

01:07:48.700 --> 01:07:54.860
I guess I'll always love you no matter what you do.
But you spoiled something.

01:07:55.200 --> 01:07:58.160
Something is gone that we'll never get back.

01:07:58.160 --> 01:08:03.440
[Charlie:] I'll try and make up for it.

01:08:05.800 --> 01:08:11.300
[Howard:] I know this town Ben. 
I doubt that we'll pull it off tomorrow night.

01:08:11.300 --> 01:08:13.266
Oh, I'm not condemning the people of Melton.

01:08:13.266 --> 01:08:15.766
They’re as decent and intelligent as any people 
anywhere,

01:08:15.766 --> 01:08:18.899
but they've been led up the garden path by our 
opponents.

01:08:18.900 --> 01:08:23.133
[Ellen:] Mrs. Jamison asked me today if you would be jailed if you didn't have a blood test certificate.

01:08:23.133 --> 01:08:26.699
[Howard:] You see a fine kindly women, 
she's been made to fear us.

01:08:26.700 --> 01:08:31.460
[Marian:] Howard dear, you've done your best, 
you, and Ben and the others.

01:08:31.460 --> 01:08:37.400
Now if you are turned down tomorrow, you'll have 
to start a long slow campaign, but you will do it.

01:08:37.400 --> 01:08:38.900
We’ll all do it.

01:08:38.900 --> 01:08:42.133
Now please, try to relax and have a pleasant 
evening.

01:08:42.133 --> 01:08:47.099
[Howard:] You're right as usual.
[Daphne:] Through here?

01:08:47.100 --> 01:08:52.900
[Marian:] Yes, thank you, Daphne.
Go home, they’ve postponed the weeding.

01:08:52.900 --> 01:08:56.366
[Daphne:] Bad luck.Take Hester Thompson for instance.

01:08:56.366 --> 01:08:59.132
All set to marry in November 1919.

01:08:59.133 --> 01:09:02.899
Hester's Ma got the flu, so had to put the wedding 
off till after Christmas.

01:09:02.900 --> 01:09:06.533
Come January, Alex's store burnt down,
had to put the date off till June.

01:09:06.533 --> 01:09:12.599
Come June, Hester fell down, broke her leg.
Well sir, from then on, just one thing after another.

01:09:12.600 --> 01:09:15.200
Got so bad, Alek took to drink.

01:09:15.200 --> 01:09:19.466
Hester took to consulting the stars,
trying to find a favorable day.

01:09:19.466 --> 01:09:21.900
Them two still ain't married.

01:09:22.780 --> 01:09:27.520
Hope there's no such backing and stalling 
when Ben and Ellen get married.

01:09:27.533 --> 01:09:29.233
[Dr. Ben:] Daphne!

01:09:29.233 --> 01:09:35.933
[Howard:] Saved by the bell, eh Ben?
Hello?

01:09:35.933 --> 01:09:40.666
Oh hello, Curran.
Yes, I imagine that's all right.

01:09:40.666 --> 01:09:42.360
Just a minute.

01:09:43.000 --> 01:09:46.100
Curran wants to see you and me in your office tonight.

01:09:46.100 --> 01:09:47.440
[Dr. Ben:] Tell him yes.

01:09:47.680 --> 01:09:52.200
[Howard:] Hello Curran.Yes, that would be all right. About half an hour.

01:09:53.440 --> 01:09:54.440
Right.

01:09:55.400 --> 01:09:56.540
[Marian:] What does Curran want?

01:09:56.720 --> 01:10:01.040
[Howard:] I don't know? Said he just had to see us.

01:10:01.100 --> 01:10:02.760
[Dr. Ben:] Well, let's go and find out.

01:10:02.766 --> 01:10:05.399
[Marian:] Maybe it's a trick.
Maybe you shouldn't go.

01:10:05.400 --> 01:10:07.760
[Dr. Ben:] I don't think it’s anything like that.

01:10:15.280 --> 01:10:18.733
Well, Mr. Curran, take a chair.
[Mr. Curran:] I'll stand.

01:10:18.733 --> 01:10:20.299
I haven't much to say.

01:10:20.300 --> 01:10:22.666
[Dr. Ben:] As you like.

01:10:22.666 --> 01:10:25.266
[Mr. Curran:] I came to give you something.

01:10:25.266 --> 01:10:29.999
Carter, I want you to swear you won't open this 
or try to find out what’s in it for two weeks.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:32.700
[Howard:] Can I decently and honestly make that 
promise?

01:10:32.700 --> 01:10:35.133
[Mr. Curran:] I give you my word, for what it's worth.

01:10:35.133 --> 01:10:38.166
[Howard:] Very well, I'll do as you say.

01:10:38.166 --> 01:10:39.666
[Mr. Curran:] One more thing.

01:10:39.666 --> 01:10:43.332
Don't bring up your health program tomorrow 
night. You'll kill it if you do.

01:10:43.333 --> 01:10:44.899
[Dr. Ben:] We're prepared to risk that.

01:10:44.900 --> 01:10:47.433
[Mr. Curran:] Don't bring it up. Get it postponed.

01:10:47.440 --> 01:10:48.940
[Howard:] I'm not going to let you win that easily.

01:10:49.220 --> 01:10:53.360
[Mr. Curran:] I don't want to win anymore. I won't oppose you.

01:10:53.366 --> 01:10:55.566
[Dr. Ben:] You what?
[Mr. Curran:] I won't oppose you.

01:10:55.566 --> 01:10:56.966
[Dr. Ben:] Then support us.

01:10:56.966 --> 01:10:59.666
If you do, we'll put it over tomorrow night or any 
night.

01:10:59.666 --> 01:11:00.499
The whole town....

01:11:00.500 --> 01:11:03.260
[Mr. Curran:] Don't let the issue be
decided tomorrow night. Wait.

01:11:03.400 --> 01:11:08.100
Wait two weeks.You promised.

01:11:08.100 --> 01:11:11.580
In two weeks, that will win for you.
That's all.

01:11:18.960 --> 01:11:21.760
[Howard:] You think Marian is right, this is some 
trick?

01:11:23.100 --> 01:11:25.440
[Dr. Ben:] No, I don't think so.

01:11:25.440 --> 01:11:44.133
[Dramatic music]

01:11:44.133 --> 01:11:46.533
[Mr. Mayor:] I can't reach him.  
I've tried for an hour.

01:11:46.533 --> 01:11:47.999
We can't wait much longer.

01:11:48.000 --> 01:11:50.000
[Mr. Higgins:] Curran has never missed
a meeting in his life.

01:11:50.000 --> 01:11:53.620
[Mr. Mayor:] Yes, but he is half an hour late 
already. We'll have to go in soon.

01:11:54.060 --> 01:11:57.100
[Tom McAllister:] What do you make of it, Howard?
What's Curran up too?

01:11:57.100 --> 01:11:58.266
[Howard:] I don't know.

01:11:58.266 --> 01:12:03.700
Look Mac, if things appear to be going against us,
let's press for a postponement

01:12:03.700 --> 01:12:07.333
on the grounds the committee hasn't completed its study, right?

01:12:07.333 --> 01:12:09.933
[Tom McAllister:] Well, I thought you were all
for going ahead tonight.

01:12:09.940 --> 01:12:11.720
[Howard:] I've changed my mind.
Got a hunch.

01:12:13.000 --> 01:12:17.460
[Mr. Mayor:] We go in.
We can't wait any longer.

01:12:17.466 --> 01:12:26.366
[Audience claps]

01:12:26.366 --> 01:12:30.640
[Mr. Mayor:] Citizens of Melton, welcome to this annual meeting.

01:12:34.500 --> 01:12:37.833
Gentlemen of the council, this is our agenda for 
this evening.

01:12:37.833 --> 01:12:41.233
The minutes of the last meeting, street lighting in ward three,

01:12:41.233 --> 01:12:45.566
the resurfacing of Hawthorne Street, and the report from the special committee

01:12:45.566 --> 01:12:47.966
to discuss community health.....

01:12:47.966 --> 01:12:51.099
[Groans from those in attendance]

01:12:51.100 --> 01:12:56.233
[Mr. Mayor:] [Slams gavel]  Please abstain from 
these outbursts.

01:12:56.240 --> 01:13:06.440
This meeting must proceed with decorum.
Gentlemen, we will proceed with our business.

01:13:17.340 --> 01:13:33.180
[A telephone lies off the hook; packed suitcases are seen.]

01:13:33.180 --> 01:13:35.960
[Mr. Curran:] How much time have we got?
[Patsy:] Not much, about twenty minutes.

01:13:35.960 --> 01:13:38.320
Why isn't Shorty here?

01:13:39.366 --> 01:13:44.660
[Mr. Curran:] I called him only for the last minute.
What time is it?

01:13:44.660 --> 01:13:48.500
[Patsy:] About six after nine.
We should be going.

01:13:50.240 --> 01:13:53.760
[Mr. Curran:] I don't want to get 
to the station too soon.

01:13:56.220 --> 01:13:58.060
Switch on the radio.

01:13:59.500 --> 01:14:01.900
I want to hear what's going on at the town hall.

01:14:08.400 --> 01:14:11.760
[Mr. Mayor:] That concludes the public works 
report.

01:14:11.766 --> 01:14:14.732
[Tom McAllister:] I move the department secure 
tenders for the painting job.

01:14:14.733 --> 01:14:17.966
[Mr. Higgins:] Second.
[Mr. Mayor:] Got it.

01:14:17.966 --> 01:14:20.599
And now we come to the special committee report.

01:14:20.600 --> 01:14:24.533
[Mr. Higgins:] Mr. Mayor, before hearing the report,
I wish to register...

01:14:24.533 --> 01:14:25.766
[Tom McAllister:] Council is out of order.

01:14:25.766 --> 01:14:30.540
[Mr. Higgins:] Register my strong disapproval of the tactics used by Councilman Carter

01:14:30.540 --> 01:14:34.433
and his crowd of busybodies in bypassing the authority of this council.

01:14:34.433 --> 01:14:35.699
[Tom McAllister:] The councilman is out of order.

01:14:35.700 --> 01:14:38.866
[Mr. Higgins:] We appointed a committee 
to study the proposed plan.

01:14:38.866 --> 01:14:44.666
Until that committee acted and council acted,
no one should have stirred up a public furor.

01:14:44.666 --> 01:14:48.832
[Howard:] There is some justice to what the 
councilor says, but there was no furor at all

01:14:48.833 --> 01:14:52.366
until the health program was attacked so 
maliciously and unfairly.

01:14:52.366 --> 01:14:55.666
[Crowd reacts]

01:14:55.666 --> 01:14:57.999
[Mr. Mayor:] If this meeting cannot be conducted 
with restraint,

01:14:58.000 --> 01:15:00.300
the council will have to adjourn to the city hall.

01:15:00.300 --> 01:15:01.533
[Mr. Higgins:] I protest.

01:15:01.533 --> 01:15:04.766
Mr. Mayor, these people are vitally concerned in 
this issue.

01:15:04.766 --> 01:15:07.500
I think it should be settled in their presence.

01:15:07.620 --> 01:15:11.640
[Clapping]

01:15:11.640 --> 01:15:14.400
[Mr. Mayor:] Well, I only thought...

01:15:14.400 --> 01:15:18.740
Certainly we must have order... orderly procedure.

01:15:18.740 --> 01:15:23.700
I will refresh your memories on the brief submitted 
to council by a panel.

01:15:23.700 --> 01:15:26.466
[Woman in crowd:] Don't bother.
[Another woman:] We know it by heart.

01:15:26.466 --> 01:15:31.266
[Mr. Mayor:] Are the councilors sufficiently familiar
with the brief?

01:15:31.266 --> 01:15:34.432
Very well, in the absence of the committee 
chairman...

01:15:34.440 --> 01:15:36.440
[Someone shouts:] Yeah, where's Curran?

01:15:36.900 --> 01:15:41.460
[Mr. Mayor:] In the absence of Councilor Curran, 
I will report for the committee.

01:15:41.460 --> 01:15:43.140
[Tom McAllister:] Mr. Mayor, you know as well as  I do

01:15:43.220 --> 01:15:46.860
that the committee was stalled by Councilor Curran each time it met.

01:15:46.866 --> 01:15:49.332
Three times in all. There's nothing to report.

01:15:49.333 --> 01:15:51.933
[Mr. Higgins:] Then why is the subject on the 
agenda?

01:15:51.933 --> 01:15:54.433
[Howard:] I move it be deferred for at least two weeks.

01:15:54.433 --> 01:15:56.233
[Mr. Mayor:] No one to second it.
[Tom McAllister:] I second it.

01:15:56.233 --> 01:15:58.166
[Audience mumbles no.]

01:15:58.166 --> 01:16:01.832
[Mr. Williams:] Whatsa matter, you afraid to discuss this crackpot scheme?

01:16:01.833 --> 01:16:05.933
[Mr. Mayor:] Under the circumstances,
I feel it is wise to defer discussion.

01:16:05.940 --> 01:16:09.140
[Mr. Williams] Where's Curran? 
Have you got him locked up somewhere?

01:16:09.260 --> 01:16:19.833
[Audience shouts, "We want Curran."]

01:16:19.840 --> 01:16:25.100
[From radio: "Mr. Mayor, I heartily concur with this 
audience’s feelings."]

01:16:26.640 --> 01:16:29.980
[Mr. Higgins:] I think the matter should be 
hashed out here and now.

01:16:33.840 --> 01:16:35.940
[Shorty:] All set Boss?

01:16:36.940 --> 01:16:39.866
[From radio: "Where's Curran, I want to hear what he has to say!"]

01:16:39.866 --> 01:16:46.132
[Shorty:] Come on, boss, ain't got much time.
[Patsy:] Come on, dad. Hurry up, snap out of it.

01:16:46.133 --> 01:16:47.966
[Mr. Curran:] I'm not going to the station.

01:16:47.966 --> 01:16:49.766
[Patsy:] Dad!

01:16:49.766 --> 01:17:04.360
[Audience shouts, "We want Curran."]

01:17:04.640 --> 01:17:29.040
[Music]

01:17:29.040 --> 01:17:31.233
[Mr. Williams:] Here's the man that knows the 
score.

01:17:31.240 --> 01:17:35.840
[Mr. Higgins:] I'd like to hear what Councilor Curran has to say about this health program.

01:17:37.240 --> 01:17:40.366
[Mr. Curran:] I think it’s the only thing for Melton.

01:17:40.366 --> 01:17:45.660
I found that out, hoped you'd find it out, too
in a couple of weeks.

01:17:45.660 --> 01:17:47.540
But never mind that.

01:17:47.540 --> 01:17:52.900
Last night, I gave Councilor Carter a sealed envelope with instructions to open it in two weeks.

01:17:52.900 --> 01:17:56.200
That was to give me time to make a getaway.

01:17:56.200 --> 01:17:58.060
Read it to them!

01:17:58.180 --> 01:18:02.680
This should prove to you that....
Well, you'll hear.

01:18:13.060 --> 01:18:16.760
[Howard:] I wish to declare that I make this 
statement of my own free will

01:18:16.766 --> 01:18:19.166
and in a normal state of mind.

01:18:19.166 --> 01:18:24.620
For nine years, I have plundered the city of Melton, 
in partnership with Marty Williams.

01:18:24.620 --> 01:18:30.120
Therefore, I associate myself in every respect 
with the charges I lay against Williams.

01:18:30.580 --> 01:18:35.380
He is owner of a gambling house and 
boardinghouse at 140 Park Drive Way.

01:18:35.380 --> 01:18:37.520
[Mr. Williams:] That's a lie!

01:18:38.500 --> 01:18:41.633
[Howard:] He sells liquor illegally in his club.

01:18:41.640 --> 01:18:45.500
He cooperates with the editor of the Magpie 
in a blackmail racket.

01:18:45.500 --> 01:18:48.960
Williams and I paid the editor of the Magpie 
one thousand dollars

01:18:48.966 --> 01:18:51.366
to discredit the health program.

01:18:51.366 --> 01:18:56.332
We also paid men to start a whispering campaign against the program.

01:18:56.333 --> 01:19:01.633
I suggest to the citizens of Melton that
they either jail Williams or run him out of town.

01:19:01.640 --> 01:19:03.400
I've removed myself.

01:19:04.060 --> 01:19:07.940
Neither of us have done anything but harm 
to this community.

01:19:08.020 --> 01:19:12.100
I hope this statement convinces you that the 
opposition to the health program was artificial from

01:19:12.100 --> 01:19:15.840
[?], so far as its beginnings are concerned.

01:19:16.140 --> 01:19:21.460
I suggest those of you who honestly oppose the scheme reconsider your objections

01:19:21.460 --> 01:19:26.380
free from the influence of such as Williams and 
myself.

01:19:29.260 --> 01:19:33.400
[Mr. Curran:] I swear this is true, so help me God.

01:19:33.520 --> 01:19:52.440
[Music]

01:19:52.440 --> 01:20:08.220
[Newspaper headlines about the scandal.]

01:20:10.200 --> 01:20:12.860
[Howard:] Well, I'll never understand it.

01:20:12.860 --> 01:20:16.120
It doesn't add up. Not for Curran.

01:20:16.920 --> 01:20:20.840
Conscience? Impossible.

01:20:22.200 --> 01:20:24.833
[Dr. Ben:] Perhaps not.
[Marian:] It was a brave thing to do.

01:20:24.833 --> 01:20:29.466
[Howard:] Oh, it took courage.
Well Ben, what's the next move?

01:20:29.466 --> 01:20:32.132
[Daphne:] Got the next move all figured out.

01:20:32.133 --> 01:20:36.199
What with all these meeting and stuff, you still ain't fixed that laundry tub.

01:20:36.200 --> 01:20:37.633
Wash day tomorrow.

01:20:37.640 --> 01:20:41.440
[Howard:] Well, then I'd better get busy on them.

01:20:42.140 --> 01:20:44.500
[Daphne:] Ain't laid out what you want washed yet.

01:20:44.500 --> 01:20:47.700
[Marian:] Of course, sorry. I'll do it right away.
[Ellen:] I'll help you mother.

01:20:47.700 --> 01:20:48.880
[Daphne:] No need.

01:20:51.760 --> 01:20:55.400
[Daphne:] No becking and stalling, Ben Edwards.

01:20:55.620 --> 01:22:12.340
[Music]

